<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
  <!ENTITY name      "cannonadecommand">
  <!ENTITY slug      "cannonadecommand">
  <!ENTITY author    "Junker der Provinz">
  <!ENTITY version   "4.28.0">
  <!ENTITY gitURL    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/junkerderprovinz/cannonadecommand/main/plugin">
  <!ENTITY pluginURL "&gitURL;/&slug;.plg">
  <!ENTITY pkgURL    "https://github.com/junkerderprovinz/cannonadecommand/releases/download/v&version;">
  <!ENTITY emhttp    "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&slug;">
  <!ENTITY plgPath   "/boot/config/plugins/&slug;">
  <!ENTITY txz       "&slug;-&version;-x86_64-1.txz">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&name;"
        author="&author;"
        version="&version;"
        pluginURL="&pluginURL;"
        min="6.10.0"
        support="https://forums.unraid.net/">

<!-- FanCtrlPlus convention: the name is the lowercase slug so Unraid resolves the
     logo (plugins/<slug>/images/<slug>.png) AND the Plugins-tab description
     (plugins/<slug>/README.md). The pretty "CannonadeCommand" name is in README.md. -->
<ICON>
/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&slug;/images/&slug;.png
</ICON>

<CHANGES>
### 4.28.0
**🎨 Design**
- Every control in the **Startplan** window is in GlimStone and in all three colour modes now, not just the ones that had been reported. The window was audited end to end and each of its controls checked in Normal, Rainbow and Flag: the **checkboxes**, the **activation toggle**, the **Save** button, the **+ Zeitplan** button, the **day chips** in a schedule, the **time field**, the window **✕**, every text and number field, every dropdown and every info bubble.
- The checkboxes were the last controls in the window still drawn by the operating system, tinted with an accent. They are the plugin's own checkbox now, in the shape the Badge-Form asks for, and each takes its own position in the palette. The tick carries its own contrast colour, so it stays readable on a pale palette entry such as the white stripe of a flag, where a white tick used to vanish.
- The **selected days** of a schedule were painted one fixed violet in Rainbow and in Flag alike, a colour that appears in no palette either mode can produce. Each chip now takes its own palette position, and the hover of an unselected chip does too instead of stepping to a flat grey.
- The **Save** button sat on a single shared colour for a whole window and could never rotate, because the fill was written directly onto the element where no colour-mode rule could reach it. So did **+ Zeitplan**, frozen on one grey with a hover that only brightened it. Both read the normal colour chain now, in the Startplan window and in the CPU/RAM and bandwidth windows with them.
- The **activation toggle** ("Im Startplan verwalten") took the one shared rainbow colour rather than its own, because the rule for toggles inside a window outranked the general one. It rotates with everything else now.
- A toggle's knob takes its track's contrast colour instead of always being white. With a palette that contains white the switch had turned into a blank capsule with an invisible knob. This applies to the settings page too, which had the same case waiting.
- The checkboxes on the **CannonadeCommand settings page** are the same plugin checkbox now, and each keeps wearing its own badge's colour rather than one flat accent.
- A field's focus is a step in brightness, as the rest of the plugin does it. The old accent ring had been silently swallowed for so long that it never appeared at all.

**✨ Added**
- The **time picker** in a schedule is the plugin's own now. A time field expands into the browser's drop-down, which cannot be styled, so picking a time opened a light panel over the dark window. It is now the same panel with the same chips as the "Hängt ab von" list in that window, two columns, every hour and every minute, and in the colour modes with everything else. Typing a time into the field works exactly as before, and the field itself is dark: the pale block the browser drew over the selected digits is gone.

**🐛 Fixed**
- Picking a container in **Hängt ab von** no longer closes the whole Startplan editor and discards every other unsaved change in it. The list is drawn outside the window, since anything else would clip it, so choosing an entry counted as a click on the page behind. This is the same failure a schedule row's ✕ had in 4.27.0, now closed for every panel a window opens rather than one widget at a time.
- A schedule row added after the window was already open no longer differs from the rows that were there when it opened. It was skipping the pass that pins the field sizes and the pass that assigns the colours, so its time field came out 116px wide against the 100px of every other row, with the Unraid theme's spacing back on it and no colour-mode colour anywhere in it.
- The clock symbol in the time field no longer disappears while the field is being typed in.

### 4.27.1
**🐛 Fixed**
- The **Array-Datenträger** list while the array is **stopped**: only the slots that actually hold a device carried a name badge. Unraid writes the slot label as a link only when a device is assigned, and every empty slot (an unused data slot, and a second parity slot that was never filled) prints it as plain text instead, so the badged and the unbadged rows sat in the same column. Measured on a 24-slot array here: 7 of 25 rows badged, 18 not. Every slot is a badge now, assigned or not, and a slot flagged *Missing* or *Wrong* keeps that note outside its badge where it belongs.
- The identification field no longer paints across the temperature column. Unraid pins that dropdown to a fixed 440px whatever its column is actually worth (218px here), keeps it clipped while the pointer is elsewhere and then unclips the whole cell on hover, so the tail of the serial, the device name in brackets and the control's own underline landed on top of the temperature badge and ran on out of the table. The field fits its column now, and the full "model, serial, size, device" line is shown in the usual hover bubble instead of on top of the neighbouring column.
- The blank bar between the parity block and the data block is gone. Unraid separates the two with an empty row that shares its class with the totals bar, so it inherited the totals bar's tint and rendered as a grey slab across the full width with nothing in it. It is a plain gap now. The totals bar and the **Slots** row carry content and keep their bar.
- The identification dropdown reads as one control again. It was being swapped for the plugin's own dropdown, but that table rebuilds itself once a second and takes the replacement with it, so a row showed one or the other depending on the moment, and a slot with no free device left to offer was never swapped at all. The look was the smaller half of it: an open list was torn out from under the pointer mid-click, on the one control in the whole interface that assigns disks. Those dropdowns stay native there now and are styled directly, so nothing can be pulled away while it is being used.

### 4.27.0
**🐛 Fixed**
- Creating a schedule in the **Startplan** editor no longer pushes the Save button off the screen. Adding a schedule row makes the window taller, but the window was placed once and only once, when it opened, so it grew downwards from a position that had only ever been right for its old height and walked off the bottom edge. With the page behind it pinned there was then no way left to reach Save at all. Measured on a 760px-tall screen: the window went from 615px to 744px and its bottom edge landed at 812px, below the screen, with the whole button row out of sight. The window is now re-placed whenever its content changes size, so it always sits fully on screen and the button row stays reachable, and the extra height goes into the scrolling part between the title and the buttons where it belongs. The page behind it stays pinned, which is the entire point of a window: unpinning it would hand back the bug 4.26.0 fixed.
- A window that stands while the browser window is resized re-places itself too.
- Removing a schedule row with its ✕ no longer closes the whole editor and discards every other unsaved change in it. The row was detached from the window before the "did that click land outside the window?" test ran, so a row's own ✕ read as a click on the page behind.

**🎨 Design**
- Every dropdown list in the plugin follows the colour modes now. CC grew four dropdown replacements, one per area, and only one of them had ever been wired into Normal, Rainbow and Flag. The other three were never given a colour at all, so every entry in them fell back to one flat accent whatever the mode was set to: the 7 lists inside the Startplan, CPU/RAM and bandwidth windows, the 11 on the CannonadeCommand settings page, the 16 on a share's settings page, and the ones on the Add-Container form. Each entry now takes its own position in the palette, exactly like the lists that already did, and the reactive sub-mode rests them neutral until the pointer reaches them.
- **Hängt ab von** in the Startplan editor was the list that had never been given the CC look at all: bare text rows on a flat slab, a grey hover, a coloured tick on the picked ones, and a fixed corner radius that ignored the Badge-Form. It is the same panel with the same chips as every other CC dropdown now, and in the colour modes with them.
- The closed box of those lists takes the colour mode on hover and while its list is open, instead of merely brightening, which looked the same in all three modes.
- All of them are coloured by one routine, in the one file that loads on every page, so an area can no longer be given the treatment while another is missed.
- **Werkzeuge** has a wrench again. 4.26.0 gave it three sliders because Tabler ships no wrench in either its outline or its filled set; the glyph now comes from FontAwesome, which the Unraid interface already loads on every page, so nothing new is pulled in for it.
- **Docker** carries the official Docker logo. 4.26.0 used a pair of boxes as a stand-in, after Tabler's own whale turned into a smudge when filled. The real brand mark was the open question at menu-bar size, so it was measured rather than assumed: rendered at the 16px the bar actually paints, the whale and its stack read cleanly and stay distinct from every neighbouring tab.

### 4.26.0
**🎨 Design**
- Every icon in the plugin is now a **filled** shape instead of an outline drawing. An outline icon is a line drawn around a form, which is the same thing CC already refuses to do to a box, only applied to a symbol. This is now a written rule in the shared design language, so it holds for everything added from here on.
- The eleven icons in the main menu bar moved from Tabler's outline set to Tabler's filled set. Six had a filled twin of the same symbol and simply swapped: Übersicht, Favoriten, Einstellungen, Plugins, VMs and Apps. Five had none, and each took the nearest filled symbol from the same set: **Start** is now a stack of discs (there is no filled server icon, and the tab is the array), **Freigaben** two folders, **Docker** a pair of boxes, **Werkzeuge** three sliders and **Stats** a filled area chart. Every candidate was rendered at 16, 20, 24 and 40px before it was picked, because a symbol that only reads at poster size is no use in a 16px menu bar.
- Docker's own whale mark has no filled version anywhere in the set, and filling the outline drawing directly turns it into an unreadable smudge. Two boxes carry the meaning at menu-bar size instead.
- The little gear on the CPU, RAM and BW buttons is filled too, in both the Docker and the VMs tab. It also changed source: it was the only icon in the plugin drawn from a different icon library, so every symbol in CC now comes from one set.
- The (i) info bubbles are one thing again. There were four separate implementations of them across the plugin, drawn at slightly different sizes, and one of them was not the same component at all: inside the Startplan window the (i) was a character on a disc that turned accent-coloured on hover and opened its explanation as a child of the row it sat in. It had no Escape, no keyboard close, and it could swallow a click meant for the field underneath. All four now build the identical filled (i), stay neutral, and open the one shared explanation bubble that is drawn over the whole page and can never be clipped by the window it lives in.
- Escape now closes an open explanation bubble. The design language has asked for that from the start and the plugin never did it, so anyone reaching an (i) by keyboard had no way to dismiss it.

**⚡ Improved**
- The Docker tab no longer scrolls away behind an open window. Opening the **Startplan** editor, or the CPU/RAM or bandwidth editor, pins the page until the window is closed, and every way of closing it (the ✕, Escape, a click beside it, the same badge again, saving, leaving the page) releases it.
- Because the page can no longer be scrolled to reach a window that runs past the bottom edge, the window now takes care of that itself: it can never open partly off-screen, and if it is taller than the screen the title and the button row stay pinned while only the part between them scrolls. Verified on a 620px-tall window: the whole editor stays reachable without the page behind it moving a pixel.
- The last four native dropdown lists in the interface — the CPU tile's timescale and the network tile's interface, view and timescale on Übersicht — are CC dropdowns now. Everywhere else this had been done long ago; these four sat on the one page the replacement had never been switched on for, so their opened list was still a plain operating-system menu. Measured across every tab afterwards: no native dropdown left anywhere.
- A CC dropdown whose underlying list is refilled by the page behind it now rebuilds instead of quietly going on offering the old entries.

### 4.25.3
**🐛 Fixed**
- The per-row Autostart toggles in the Docker tab follow the Badge-Form again. With the form set to **Abgerundet**, every other element on the page sat at a 6px radius while the 52 Autostart switches stayed hard pills, and **Eckig** did not square them either.
- The cause was the speed-up that shipped in 4.24.0. Skipping Unraid's switch widget and styling the bare checkbox instead was the right call for the freeze it removed, but the replacement was drawn with a fixed pill radius baked in. The widget it replaced had been reading the shape setting all along, so the shape simply stopped arriving the moment the faster path took over.
- Track and knob now both read the shape setting, capped at half their own size so the switch can go the whole way from pill through rounded to a clean square without the knob ever outgrowing its track. Measured live at all four settings: Pille and Kreis give 999px, Abgerundet 6px, Eckig 0px, matching the badges beside them exactly.
- The old widget path was given the same treatment. It is unreachable while theming is on, but leaving a hardcoded radius sitting in a rule that still matches is how this came back the first time.

### 4.25.2
**🐛 Fixed**
- State dots are green again when everything is fine. 4.25.1 got them showing a colour again, but the colour it gave them was the colour mode's, not the container's — and that is one single page-wide value, so every dot came out the same. Measured on a live tab: 38 running, 11 exited and 9 created containers all rendered the identical blue. A stopped container and a running one were indistinguishable, which is the one thing a status light must never be.
- Both Docker-tab dots (the running/stopped dot under the container name and its twin beside the Startplan badge) now keep their native state colour in every colour mode: green running, grey stopped, amber paused, red dead or unhealthy.
- The same fix reached the disk state orbs on the Übersicht tab, which had the identical problem one step worse — ten healthy drives and seven empty slots were all resting on the same grey. Healthy drives read green there again.
- Why this is no longer tied to a setting: **Zustandsanzeigen nativ färben** still decides the question for usage bars and status badges, and it should — a bar carries its value in its length and a badge carries its in its text, so their colour is a second voice that can safely join the palette. A state dot has no text and no length. Colour is all it has, so it is not a styling choice any more than legible text is. The toggle's description was updated to say so.

### 4.25.1
**🐛 Fixed**
- The two state indicators in the Docker tab — the container running/stopped dot under the name and its twin beside the Startplan badge — show their colour again. They had been pulled into the reactive sub-mode's rest state, so they sat on a flat grey and only took a colour while the pointer happened to be on their row. Resting a state indicator at neutral empties it of meaning: unlike a badge or a button, its colour *is* the information. They now keep the colour-mode colour at all times, in every sub-mode. Native state colours are still one toggle away under "Zustandsanzeigen nativ färben".

**⚡ Improved**
- The **Mehrfachauswahl** button in the bottom action bar now sits directly right of **Containergröße** instead of being flung to the far end of the bar behind the view toggle, and it is finally the same button as its neighbours: same height, text size, casing, letter spacing, padding, corner shape and spacing (it was a small mixed-case chip: 21px vs 30px high, 11px vs 13px text). It also takes its own slot in the bar's colour rotation, so no two adjacent buttons share a colour. While multi-select is switched on the button reads as pressed in every colour mode.

### 4.25.0
**🐛 Fixed**
- Section badges, title badges and the bottom buttons now actually follow the colour modes in **every** process window (container update, template-edit recreate, and the iframe update dialog). They used to fall back to one single shared colour, so a four-step update window painted its title, all four step badges and its button in the same flat tone while the rest of the UI rotated through the palette; each badge and button now takes its own palette position, rotating continuously through the window. Applies to Normal, Rainbow and Flag alike.
- Flag mode: flag colours no longer collapse. A readability guard meant to hide a near-black palette slot (the German flag's black stripe) was set so aggressively that it also swallowed legitimately dark flag colours — the Algerian flag's green scored a hair under the limit, so every green badge was replaced with white and the window rendered white/white/red instead of the flag's green/white/red cycle.
- The iframe update dialog ignored the colour modes entirely: it painted its badges and buttons from a single fixed accent that never looked at the rainbow/flag colour at all.

**⚡ Improved**
- Both process windows are now always the same size instead of shrinking to fit their content — a short recreate used to render a much smaller window than a long update (measured: 735px vs 1219px on the same screen). A window with fewer cards keeps its full size, and more content than fits simply scrolls inside it as before. The button row stays pinned to the bottom edge either way.

### 4.24.3
**🐛 Fixed**
- Container-update window: a leftover "Cancel" button from the confirm step could pop back up between the status indicator and "Fertig" (Unraid hides it inline, but an existing CC rule was overriding that with `!important`), inconsistently rearranging the button row.
- Template-edit recreate window: the gap between the title badge and the first section badge was noticeably tighter than the real update window's (matched to the same measured spacing); the title badge now gets its own colour-mode colour like the real window's does, instead of flatly matching the section badges below it.

### 4.24.2
**🐛 Fixed**
- Template-edit recreate window (Edit → Apply): fixed several remaining mismatches against the real update window found by measuring both windows directly — it rendered at half the real window's width (a `rem`-based size cap resolved differently because the two pages use different root font sizes), every log card showed a permanent scrollbar from a 1px sub-pixel rounding artifact, and the button row carried a shadow the real window never has.
- Same window: section badges rendered oversized because an unrelated Tools-page stylesheet was incorrectly also styling this page's fieldsets; the status indicator now sits beside the "Fertig" button like the real window instead of floating under the title.

### 4.24.1
**🐛 Fixed**
- Applying a template edit (Edit → Apply, which removes and recreates the container) now shows the exact same styled window as a real image update — its title badge used to sit inset with visible margin instead of spanning edge-to-edge like the update window.

### 4.24.0
**⚡ Improved**
- Docker tab is noticeably less frozen after a container update/start/stop/remove finishes — the per-row Autostart switch no longer rebuilds itself with a heavy jQuery widget on every refresh, cutting the freeze after closing the update window by roughly 60% on a host with many containers (looks and behaves exactly the same, just built without the extra weight).

### 4.23.1
**🐛 Fixed**
- Container-update window: a horizontal scrollbar no longer flashes at the start of an update — the streamed log forced `white-space:pre` (needed for the ASCII banner), which never wraps a long unbroken progress line; switched to `pre-wrap` so normal lines render identically and only an actually-too-wide line wraps.

### 4.23.0
**✨ Added**
- Folder view: a "move to folder" button on every card opens a menu listing every folder — pick one to file the container there, no drag required.
- Folder view: drag a container onto a folder (or the open background) to move it there; drag a folder you created onto another to reorder them.

**🐛 Fixed**
- Settings → Docker-Tab → Standard-Ansicht: picking Grid or Folder now actually survives a reload — the picker only ever saved locally before, so it was silently overridden by whatever CC last remembered on the server.

### 4.22.0
**✨ Added**
- Docker tab: new "Folder" view alongside List and Grid, built on Unraid's own native Docker Organizer — group containers into folders right from CC.
- Create, rename and delete folders directly from the Folder view. A folder made by another tool (e.g. FolderView3) stays untouched — CC only ever manages folders it created itself, and always moves a folder's containers back out before deleting it, never dropping them.
- The chosen Docker-tab view (List/Grid/Folder) now syncs across browsers and devices — it's saved server-side, not just in this one browser.

**🎨 Design**
- Settings → Docker-Tab → Standard-Ansicht: added "Ordner" as a third option alongside Liste/Raster.
- List view now also styles container rows nested inside a folder by another Docker-organizer plugin, matching the normal row look instead of appearing unstyled.

### 4.21.0
**🐛 Fixed**
- App-info popup: section badges are colourful again in every colour mode — they're plain non-interactive labels with no hover state, so the previous release's neutral-until-hover treatment just left them permanently washed out.
- App-info popup: the Support and Pin App buttons now actually react to the colour mode on hover, matching every other button.
- App-info popup: the Support button's dropdown menu is now styled to match the rest of the popup instead of rendering as a plain native list.

**🎨 Design**
- App-info popup: the Support button no longer shows an icon, just the label.
- App-info popup: the Pin App button is now a pin icon instead of text.
- App-info popup: on Spotlight apps, "Why we picked it" now shows in the star badge's own tooltip instead of a separate info bubble next to it.

### 4.20.0
**🐛 Fixed**
- App-info popup: section badges (Infotext, Details, Maintainer, ...) now actually follow the active colour mode — they fell back to one flat static colour before, ignoring both Rainbow's per-section jewel colours and Reactive mode's neutral-until-hover contract.
- App-info popup: removed a second, separate layer of empty space above the content — the previous release only cleared the close button's own padding, not the drawer's own 40px native top padding underneath it.
- App-info popup: the "Zusätzliche Anforderungen" card is now full width like every other card, instead of sitting indented and narrower.
- Apps tab: the left sidebar is wider so "Installierte Apps", "Bisherige Apps", "Angeheftete Apps" and "Bevorzugtes Repository" no longer wrap onto two lines.

### 4.19.0
**🐛 Fixed**
- App-info popup: the description's own "SHOW MORE" toggle is now a badge too, matching the changelog's — it was the one readmore toggle the previous pass missed.
- App-info popup: CA's own "Attention:" notice (blacklisted, incompatible, or custom-network templates) is now its own badge-card instead of CA's plain red-bordered box.
- App-info popup: removed roughly 30px of invisible padding CA's own close-button bar carried, so the drawer's content starts right under the close button instead of leaving an empty gap.
- App-info popup: badge-cards now sit further apart — the previous margins were collapsing down to a tighter gap than intended.
- App-info popup: the app grid behind the drawer no longer scrolls while the drawer is open — CA's own scroll-lock class was targeting the wrong element.

### 4.18.0
**🐛 Fixed**
- App-info popup: it now floats free of every window edge (top/right/bottom margins), matching the notification centre, instead of touching the top and right edges.
- App-info popup: the section badges no longer show a "1." / "1.1." / "2." number prefix — those were only ever meant as an internal structure guide, not for display.
- App-info popup: the Details and Maintainer cards are now always the same width and span the drawer's full width, instead of sometimes sitting side by side at partial width.
- App-info popup: the "Zusätzliche Anforderungen" card no longer shows its title twice or renders shifted — a stray leftover heading is now moved into the card together with its content instead of being left behind.
- App-info popup: Spotlight apps no longer show the round icon; "Why we picked it" now lives in an info bubble next to the star badge.

**✨ Added**
- App-info popup: the changelog, the readmore "SHOW MORE" toggle, the Donate button, and template-error notices are now their own badge-cards too, matching the rest of the popup.

### 4.17.1
**🐛 Fixed**
- Settings page version line showed the wrong GlimStone version (1.5.0) — GlimStone folded its pre-release history into a single v1.0.0, corrected here to match.

### 4.17.0
**⚡ Improved**
- Settings page version line now also shows the adopted GlimStone design-language version (UI vX.Y.Z · GlimStone vX.Y.Z · Engine ...), matching the same convention applied across every other GlimStone-adopting app.

### 4.16.0
**✨ Added**
- App-info popup redesign: now matches the notification centre's floating-window style — numbered badge-cards for each section (1. Infotext, 1.1 Zusätzliche Anforderungen when present, 2. Details, 3. Maintainer, 4. Trends when present), each section badge sitting half over its card like the update window's own cards.
- App-info popup: the close button is now a square badge with an X, always square regardless of the active badge-shape setting.
- App-info popup: Spotlight apps show a small star badge next to the app name, matching the card's own Spotlight badge.
- Both the app-info popup and the notification centre now play a "wild"-style bounce/slide entrance animation when Animationen is set to Wild.

### 4.15.0
**🐛 Fixed**
- Display Settings language dropdown: the flags weren't showing as flags for some users — Windows renders the Unicode flag emoji this used as two separate letters instead of a flag glyph. Switched to the plugin's own bundled flag images (already used elsewhere for the Flaggen-Modus colour picker), so the flag now renders identically everywhere.
- Display Settings language dropdown: five entries (Danish, Japanese, Korean, Arabic, Bengali) previously showed no flag or the wrong one, because Unraid's own locale code for them isn't a real country code — corrected to the right flag for each.
- Native Settings sub-pages (e.g. Display Settings): the bottom action buttons (Standard/Anwenden/Fertig) fell back to a hardcoded default blue instead of the actually configured accent colour whenever Rainbow/Flag mode was off — now correctly follow the configured accent everywhere.

### 4.14.0
**🐛 Fixed**
- Display Settings language dropdown: the "Verfügbar (nicht installiert)" group label at the bottom of the list is gone — the download glyph on each entry already signals that on its own.
- Display Settings language dropdown: the trailing "(German)"-style English clarification is now stripped from every entry, including the ones you already have installed.
- Display Settings language dropdown: the not-installed entries no longer carry a border — a dimmer background fill signals them instead, matching the rest of the style guide.
- Display Settings ("Anzeige-Einstellungen"): the header colour fields (text/secondary-text/background) had their colour swatch stacked above the hex input instead of beside it, and the hex field stretched far past where every dropdown on the page ends. Both now sit on one line, with the hex field's right edge lined up exactly with the dropdowns above it.
- Apps-tab card: the "..." actions menu's items (Info, Zuerst lesen, Project, Support Forum, Registry) stayed a flat neutral grey on hover regardless of the active colour mode — they now take the same accent/rainbow colour as every other interactive element on the tab.

**🌐 Translations**
- Apps-tab: the coloured section pills above each app row (Kürzlich hinzugefügt, Spotlight-Apps, Angesagte Apps, Top-Neuinstallationen, Beliebteste Plugins, Zufällige Apps, Empfohlene Anwendungen) and their info-bubble subtitles are now shown in German instead of English.
- Apps-tab sidebar: several more category labels (Sprache, Medienanwendungen, Medienserver, Netzwerkdienste, Werkzeuge, Dienstprogramme, Alle Apps, Statistiken, Änderungsprotokoll, Fehlersuche) are now translated.

### 4.13.0
**🐛 Fixed**
- Apps-tab card: the description text box was still noticeably shorter than the card actually had room for — a wrong assumption about the card's height meant every earlier pass on this box was working with 25px less space than genuinely available. Now sized against the card's real height, with equal spacing above and below.
- Apps-tab card: hovering a long, truncated app name to reveal it as scrolling text instead shifted the whole name sideways over the app icon, and never actually showed the hidden part. Fixed to scroll the text within its own fixed box.
- Apps-tab card: the new attention badge (for templates with a Community Applications notice) now follows the same accent/rainbow colour behaviour as the other corner badges, instead of always staying amber.
- Display Settings: the language dropdown's "available, not installed" entries no longer show a redundant English name in parentheses.
- Apps-tab: a number of native Community Applications sidebar and toolbar labels (section names, "Show more", results-per-page, sort options) only ever showed in English even with the display language set to German — now shown in the configured language, matching everything else on the tab.

**🎨 Design**
- Apps-tab card: the repository/maintainer line sits with a little more clearance below the app name.

### 4.12.0
**✨ Added**
- Display Settings: the Sprache/Language dropdown now lists every language pack Unraid officially offers, not just the ones already installed — picking one you don't have yet takes you straight to its Community Applications listing to install it.
- Apps-tab card: templates carrying a notice (the small comment-bubble hint Community Applications shows, e.g. driver/hardware requirements) now get a square attention badge next to the Docker/Plugin type badge, instead of a small inline icon buried in the app name.

**🐛 Fixed**
- Apps-tab card: in Reactive colour mode, hovering anywhere on a card lit up every badge on it together instead of only the one actually under the pointer.
- Apps-tab card: a long app name could run under the top-right badges instead of stopping before them. It now always stops clear of whichever badges are actually present on that card, and reveals the full name on hover.
- Apps-tab card: the description text box sits further down again, with equal spacing above (from the app name) and below (to the download/install row).

### 4.11.0
**🐛 Fixed**
- Settings could silently stop syncing across browsers/devices once you had about 60+ CC settings configured (accent colours, badge shapes, per-area toggles, column layouts, ...) — the engine capped stored settings at 64 entries and rejected anything past that with no visible error, which is very reachable for anyone who has touched most of CC's customization options. Cap raised substantially.
- That cross-browser settings sync only ever ran on the Docker tab and CC's own Settings page. Every other page (Apps, Plugins, VMs, Shares, Unraid's own Settings pages) never synced at all — now it runs everywhere.
- Native dropdown lists outside CC's Tools area (like Display Settings' own "Sprache/Language" list) rendered with no CC styling at all, since the color and shape it followed was scoped to the Tools page specifically. Now themed everywhere.
- Apps-tab card: the Spotlight badge sat much further from the Docker/Plugin type badge than intended, caused by a native attribute fighting the intended position. The download/updated/install badge row could also drift left or right depending on how many status ribbons a given card had; both groups are now independently anchored so their position never moves.

**🎨 Design**
- Docker tab: the per-row bulk-select checkboxes are now hidden by default, revealed by a new "Mehrfachauswahl" badge in the floating action bar.
- Apps-tab card: the description text box sits a little further down with equal spacing above and below it.

### 4.10.0
**🎨 Design**
- Apps-tab card: the Spotlight mark is now a square icon badge (a star) next to the Docker/Plugin type badge, with the spotlight month shown on hover instead of its own separate badge. The Official/Beta/Limited-Time ribbons moved down into the download/updated/install row, aligned to its left edge, freeing up space for a taller description text field.

### 4.9.0
**✨ Added**
- Docker tab: select several containers at once (a checkbox on each row) and start, stop or remove them together from a floating toolbar, instead of one at a time. Bulk remove shows one combined confirmation listing every selected container.
- Display Settings: the "Sprache/Language" dropdown now shows a flag next to every installed language pack.

### 4.8.0
**🐛 Fixed**
- On the Plugins tab, a plugin's "Update available" and "Up to date" status badges rendered at different sizes. The update badge is a native browser button underneath, which was carrying its own button chrome plus an unrelated sizing rule meant for a different button elsewhere on the page; both badges now share the same small-badge tokens used system-wide.

### 4.7.0
**🐛 Fixed**
- The Docker tab could freeze for several seconds after removing, updating, starting or stopping a container on a host with many containers. Root cause: a view-mode check (Basic/Advanced) was being re-derived from scratch on every single badge on every row instead of once per pass, each re-derivation forcing a synchronous style recalculation. On a host with 50+ containers this compounded into several seconds of a fully unresponsive tab; it is now computed once per pass.

### 4.6.0
**🐛 Fixed**
- A stray dark patch could appear in the middle of a card's description text, left over from Community Applications' own text-fade effect no longer lining up with this card's description box.

**🎨 Design**
- Status ribbons (OFFICIAL/BETA/SPOTLIGHT) now sit directly under the app name and maintainer instead of above the download/update badges, leaving more room for the description.
- The description shows more text and has a larger gap below the app name area.
- Download count and last-updated date badges are wider, and go back to being hidden entirely (rather than showing "N/A") when no data is available.

### 4.5.0
**🐛 Fixed**
- The Apps-tab card's menu button and Docker/Plugin type badge weren't vertically aligned with each other, and the download/update badge row wasn't flush with the row of status ribbons above it, both caused by native margins that were never reset.
- An already-installed app's card could show "Installiert" twice, once as a status ribbon and once as the badge next to Download/Update.
- The author line sat too close to the app name.

**🎨 Design**
- The description now shows a bit more text before it's clipped.
- The Docker/Plugin type badge and the "Update" state of the primary badge now pick up their own color in Rainbow mode instead of a shared flat accent.

### 4.4.0
**🐛 Fixed**
- The Apps-tab card's icon and name could render partially clipped above the top of the card, and the description sat with inconsistent, cramped spacing near the badges below it. Both were relying on the card's native layout flow, which turned out not to be reliably predictable; they now use the same fixed positioning as the rest of the card.

### 4.3.0
**✨ Added**
- The Apps-tab card's primary action button now reflects real install/update state: "Installieren" when not installed, "Update" when installed and an update is available, or "Installiert" when installed and up to date.

**🎨 Design**
- Status ribbons (OFFICIAL/BETA/SPOTLIGHT/INSTALLED) now line up in one row directly above the download/update badges instead of stacking in the top-right corner, which is now reserved for the Docker/Plugin type badge and the menu button.
- The description now scrolls with the mouse wheel while hovering instead of only sliding up by a fixed amount, so text of any length can be read in full.
- Download count and last-updated date badges always show a value now ("N/A" when unknown) at a fixed, equal width, and every badge on the card shares the same height.

### 4.2.0
**🐛 Fixed**
- The Apps-tab card's new hamburger menu button rendered noticeably wider than tall instead of a clean square, and could land far from the actual top-right corner on a card with more than one status ribbon.
- The description text and the download/update/install row could shift position unpredictably depending on a card's exact content, since they still relied on Community Applications' own native layout offsets.

**🎨 Design**
- Download count and last-updated date are now bare badges (no label text) grouped together with the Install button as a single cluster in the card's bottom-right corner.

### 4.1.0
**🎨 Design**
- Reworked the Apps-tab card layout to actually match ca.unraid.net/apps end to end: the icon now sits beside the name and maintainer instead of above them, the category tag is gone, the description scrolls upward on hover to reveal more, and the download count, last-updated month, and the Install button now share one row at the bottom.
- Info, Support, and (for an already-installed app) the Edit/Uninstall Actions menu now live in a single hamburger menu in the card's top corner instead of three separate buttons, freeing the bottom row for just the primary Install action.

### 4.0.0
**✨ Added**
- Apps-tab cards now show a download count and last-updated month, matching the layout of ca.unraid.net/apps. Community Applications' own card never renders this itself (only its Info popup does, one app at a time); read once from CA's own local catalog cache, so no extra load per card.

**🎨 Design**
- The category label on each Apps-tab card is now a filled tag pill instead of bare uppercase text.

### 3.9.4
**🐛 Fixed**
- Triggering a container update from ShipLog's changelog bubble and closing the update window afterward could freeze the whole Docker tab for several seconds with nothing clickable. Live-traced to our own decorative loading overlay: Unraid's native list refresh blocks on dockerd, which can stay busy well past the usual instant response right after a container recreate, and our overlay, painted on top of Unraid's own loading spinner for that whole wait, had no pointer-events rule, so it silently swallowed every click on the page for as long as it was up. It no longer blocks interaction.
- Hardened the engine's per-container stats/limits calls with their own timeout, so one slow-to-respond container (e.g. one that was just recreated) can no longer stall the response for every other container.

### 3.9.3
**🐛 Fixed**
- The new dependency-readiness dot (3.9.2) showed red for every dependency right after a daemon restart, even when everything was running fine — it only trusted the orchestrator's last recorded run, which is empty until the plan actually executes again. It now falls back to each dependency's live running state when there is no recorded run yet, matching how the engine's own readiness probe already treats a running container with no healthcheck as ready.

### 3.9.2
**✨ Added**
- A small state dot next to the Startplan badge (Docker tab, Autostart column) for any container that depends on others in the start plan — green when every dependency's last orchestrator run came back ready, red with a per-dependency breakdown in the tooltip otherwise. Same look as the existing running/stopped dot under the container name.

### 3.9.1
**🎨 Design**
- The Developer Sandbox confirmation button on Unraid API Settings had its own native recipe (a gradient ring implemented as a decorative layer rather than a real border, so the earlier fix for 3.9.0 never reached it) — now a plain solid red like every other destructive control.

### 3.9.0
**🎨 Design**
- The Apps tab's card badges (Info/Support/Install) now centre their text properly instead of sitting slightly high, and the sidebar search field's magnifier and clear icons no longer sit a couple of pixels off from the field's own centre.
- The App Info drawer (opened from a card's Info button) now matches the rest of the theme instead of a plain black panel with a stark white description box and unstyled buttons — dark cards, chip buttons, a dimmed details table. Its native full-width close bar, which used to float over the app grid above the drawer instead of sitting inside it, is fixed too.
- Settings > Verwaltungszugriff > Unraid API Settings and API Keys (Unraid's own newer Vue-based subtabs) now follow your configured accent colour and badge shape instead of Unraid's fixed native styling, including the toggle, buttons and the built-in Unraid.net provider pill.

**🐛 Fixed**
- Previous Apps: the bulk delete button shared a CSS class with Community Applications' own native delete handling, which could intercept the click and show CA's generic confirmation instead of the real one — sometimes leaving the delete inconsistent. It now has its own class and no longer collides.
- The Install Selected/Select all/Delete action bar at the bottom of the Apps tab is native to Community Applications and only ever works on Previous Apps (nothing else offers the checkboxes it needs) — it's hidden everywhere else now instead of sitting there permanently disabled.
- (with ShipLog installed) Its changelog bubble's buttons stayed solidly coloured even with Reactive colour mode on; they now rest neutral and only take their colour on hover, like every other control.

### 3.8.1
**🐛 Fixed**
- The Docker-tab changelog chip's close button (ShipLog integration) now follows the active colour mode too, alongside the two action buttons.
- Settings > Management Access is now fully styled — its inputs, dropdowns and toggle switches follow the active colour mode instead of sitting with default borders and native toggle colours.
- The Previous Apps page's bulk-delete button now stays disabled until at least one app is checked, is simply labelled "Delete", and no longer leaves the page scrolled to the bottom afterwards; the selection-clearing button is now labelled "Reset selection" to read less like a delete action.
- The Previous Apps bulk-delete button now reliably shows red in every colour mode instead of occasionally showing an unrelated accent colour.

### 3.8.0
**✨ Added**
- The Previous Apps page now has a real "Remove selected" button that deletes every checked app from Community Applications' history in one go, next to the existing selection-clearing button.

**🎨 Design**
- Settings > Management Access > Unraid API Status is now fully styled — the card border, colours and buttons all follow the active colour mode instead of sitting unstyled.

**🐛 Fixed**
- The account menu's info bubble now appears on hover, not only after a click.
- The VMs tab's loading spinner reliably shows again while CC paints its badges and actions over the table, instead of clearing before a single frame could render it.
- ShipLog's "Not maintained" and "Editorially deprecated" chips are no longer grey; they show red/amber like every other severity state.

### 3.7.5
**🐛 Fixed**
- Utility icons other than the bell and menu (lock, search, terminal, browse, feedback, info, log) no longer hop noticeably higher than the tabs when hovered in Wild animation mode.
- The Docker tab loading spinner reliably shows again while CC paints its badges and actions over the table, instead of clearing before a single frame could render it.
- The Boot Parameters settings page (Settings > Boot Parameters) is now fully styled — section badges, warning/info callouts, toggles and kernel-parameter chips all follow the active colour mode instead of sitting unstyled.
- Triggering a container update no longer scrolls the whole page to the bottom; only the update dialog's own log still follows along as it streams.
- The "Create API Key" modal (Settings > API Keys) opens fully on screen instead of being cut off near the top of the browser window.
- The "Create API Key" button now follows the active colour mode and matches the size of every other CC button, and no longer shows a stray dropdown arrow.
- The button that only clears the current selection on the Previous Apps page is now labelled "Clear Selection" instead of the misleading "Delete" — the actual per-app removal is the "Remove from Previous Apps" entry in each card's Actions menu.
- A redundant section label (e.g. "Previous Apps", "Installed Apps") no longer appears above the header badges on any Apps-tab subpage; this generalizes the earlier Action Centre-only fix to every section.

### 3.7.4
**⚡ Improved**
- The Docker, VMs and Plugins tabs load noticeably faster, especially with a large number of containers: several per-row and per-tick lookups that used to re-scan the whole list now resolve in constant time instead of re-scanning it.
- The tab-load spinner now stays up until CC has actually finished painting the enhanced badges and actions over the row, instead of disappearing the moment Unraid's own unstyled rows first appear, closing the brief flash of native content in between.

**🎨 Design**
- Sidebar badges now use exactly two font sizes everywhere, card title backgrounds render consistently, category members only highlight on hover instead of staying stuck highlighted, VERSION sorts after Change Log/Debugging, and every badge/card gap is a consistent 6px.
- Icon-only main tabs (label hidden) now match the size of the other header utility icons instead of keeping oversized text padding.

**🐛 Fixed**
- ShipLog's critical-risk changelog chip (a major update with a flagged breaking change) is no longer grey; it now shows red like every other severity level.
- The full-screen loading spinner on Docker/VMs/Plugins tab navigation no longer visibly jumps from a corner to the centre on appearance.
- The bell and menu icons in the top right are correctly ordered and spaced again, matching every other utility icon.
- Inner scrollbars across the WebUI are no longer forced to an oversized thickness; only the Apps-tab carousels keep the wider badge-shaped scrollbar.
- The Boot-Datenträger flyout on the Main tab no longer overlaps its own field labels, and its Anwenden/Fertig buttons stay in the correct column.
- The Apps-tab loading spinner no longer shows a stray scrollbar on its own dialog, or a brief horizontal scrollbar from the app carousels underneath it.
- Opening an unrelated popup, including ShipLog's own changelog window, no longer scrolls the whole page to the bottom.
- Clicking "Results Per Page" in the Apps sidebar no longer paints the whole search badge red.

### 3.7.3
**✨ Added**
- A second switch lets you hide the main tab text for an icon-only look (Kopfbereich settings), alongside the existing icon toggle.

**🎨 Design**
- The Apps sidebar has been rebuilt as a real badge/card system: sections (Installed Apps, Previous Apps, Pinned Apps, Categories) are cards with a coloured title badge and a shared background, while every standalone entry (Home, Search, Results Per Page, DockerHub, Action Centre, All Apps, Repositories, Settings, Statistics, Credits, Support, Version, Change Log, Debugging) is its own badge — all the same width. Category sub-items stay visibly smaller and indented under their parent category.
- The footer scroll arrows now use a solid background instead of a translucent one, so they stay legible over any page content.

**⚡ Improved**
- The bell and menu icons now re-pin on a hover anywhere on the page, not just near the icons themselves.
- The settings search button no longer drifts far to the right of the actual cards on wide windows.
- The footer scroll arrows now correctly fade out at the very top and very bottom of a page instead of staying on screen.
- "Results Per Page" no longer wraps or crowds the search badge above it.

**🐛 Fixed**
- The SHOW MORE badge on the Apps home page is no longer stuck dark regardless of colour mode.
- The search icon in the Apps sidebar badge is now properly centred next to its label.
- Sidebar badges no longer sit higher on the Action Centre page than on every other page.

### 3.7.2
**✨ Added**
- The main tab icons can now be switched off in CC's settings (Kopfbereich).

**⚡ Improved**
- The Werkzeuge-Tab in CC's settings now has a real style control, instead of just an explanatory note.
- The bell and menu icons in the top right now re-align immediately when hovered, closing a gap the periodic check alone didn't always catch in time.

**🐛 Fixed**
- The "Results per page" badge in the Apps sidebar no longer disappears on the main app grid.
- Clicking the X to reset an active search no longer reopens the search field.
- A redundant "Action Centre" label above the sidebar badges is gone.
- The update/install dialog now follows the log to the bottom as it streams, instead of staying scrolled at the top.

### 3.7.1
**✨ Added**
- The main navigation tabs (Dashboard, Docker, VMs, Plugins, ...) now show an icon next to each label.

**⚡ Improved**
- Card ribbons (Official, Spotlight, ...) on the Apps page now follow the active colour mode, each card getting its own palette colour like everything else.
- The system notice banner (e.g. "A reboot is required to apply changes") now matches the plugin's look, with colours that reflect what it's actually saying (warning, error or success) instead of native yellow.

**🐛 Fixed**
- CA's own settings page: the button rows now stay correctly aligned with the toggle column in every case.
- The relocated "Results per page" and "DockerHub" sidebar badges now match the size of every other sidebar entry, and DockerHub gets its styling correctly instead of a native, unstyled look.
- A hidden accessibility hint in the Apps search could occasionally become visible; it now stays reliably hidden.
- The bell and menu icons in the top right could occasionally disappear and reappear repeatedly; a continuous check now keeps them in place.

### 3.7.0
**✨ Added**
- A unified loading-spinner engine: every spinner in the plugin (tab switches, container/plugin dialogs, the Apps update overlay) now shares one set of size and speed tokens instead of several separate hand-built rings.
- Card shadows now follow a shared depth system with dedicated values for the light theme, instead of every card reusing shadows tuned for the dark theme.

**🎨 Design**
- The "results per page" and DockerHub search badges now sit in the sidebar next to the Apps search, instead of the top of the main content area.
- Pagination numbers and the sort-order arrows now follow the active colour mode.
- The footer's scroll-to-top and scroll-to-bottom arrows now follow the active colour mode.

**⚡ Improved**
- Turning animations off now also reaches Community Applications' own buttons, dialogs and the footer arrows, not just CannonadeCommand's own elements.
- App-card badges (the corner ribbon and the top-right badge) share one consistent size across every card.
- App-card action buttons now wrap onto a single row instead of breaking across two lines on narrower cards.

**🐛 Fixed**
- CA's own settings page ("ca_settings"): the Anwenden/Fertig and Download-Log/Hilfe button rows now correctly line up with the toggle column above them.
- The Community Applications tab no longer shows a second, unwanted "delete" button next to the real one.
- Search no longer clears what you typed when you press Enter or pick a result.
- The footer arrows no longer have two competing colour rules fighting each other depending on load order.
- The Plugins sub-navigation badge is back to its correct size.
- The "results per page" dropdown no longer opens in the wrong position after being moved into the sidebar.
- The container/plugin update dialog no longer shows two loading rings at once.
- Settings > System Temperature no longer gets stuck under a dimmed overlay after certain dialogs open.
- Colour-mode badges no longer flash their accent colour for an instant before settling on neutral when a page first loads.
- Network throughput on the Overview page now reflects true total traffic; it previously counted only one network interface and undercounted usage significantly on multi-NIC systems.

### 3.6.6
**🐛 Fixed**
- Fixed a bug from 3.6.2 that could freeze a browser tab on the Docker page under heavy system load: a self-observing watcher on the tab-load spinner could keep re-triggering itself. It now runs on a simple, time-limited check instead.

### 3.6.5
**🐛 Fixed**
- The plugin no longer disappears after a full server reboot. Unraid reinstalls every plugin very early at boot, before the network is reliably up; the plugin package is now embedded directly in the plugin file instead of being downloaded, so the reinstall no longer depends on the network at all. (v3.6.4 attempted this but had a bug that broke the install; superseded, never released as latest.)

### 3.6.3
**🐛 Fixed**
- The scroll to top and scroll to bottom arrows in the bottom right corner no longer show an underline when you hover them.

### 3.6.2
**🎨 Design**
- The Apps search is now a full width "Suche" field in the left sidebar; typing opens a larger results list and blurs the page behind it.
- The start plan editor dropdowns now use the CannonadeCommand dropdown style, matching every other select.
- The Plugins section badge is now the same size as the "Check for updates" button.
- Unraid's own scrollbars are a little thicker and follow the badge shape; the browser's native page scrollbar is left untouched.

**⚡ Improved**
- On a wide window the advanced view toggle lines up exactly with the right content edge.
- The tab loading spinner shows a single clean ring instead of a large one overlapping a small one.

**🐛 Fixed**
- Narrowing the window no longer pushes the container and plugin lists too far to the right.
- The container update window no longer shows raw stylesheet text under the title, and its buttons stay pinned at the bottom.
- The "Startnummer" info bubble now shows its explanation instead of being empty.
- The container move arrows now disappear again when you leave edit mode.
- Badges react to hover with a colour change, never an underline.

### 3.6.1
**🎨 Design**
- The Apps search now sits in the left sidebar as a badge directly under Home, instead of the top right corner.
- Page, section and sub-navigation badges are a clearly smaller step below the main menu tabs.
- App-tab scrollbars are thicker and easier to grab.

**⚡ Improved**
- On a wide window the status island, the header icons, the footer arrows and the view toggle stay lined up with
  the content edge instead of drifting off to the far right as the window grows.
- Badges respond to hover with a colour change in both colour modes, never a plain underline.

**🐛 Fixed**
- Scrollbars show the CannonadeCommand styled bar again on Chromium and Brave, without the stray end arrows.
  A recent browser change had been quietly disabling the custom scrollbar styling.
- Container-update window: the streamed style block no longer appears as raw text under the title, and the
  buttons and spinner stay pinned to the bottom of the window instead of being overlaid by the log.

### 3.6.0
**✨ Added**
- Network status island: a live download and upload throughput chip in the header. Click it to switch between
  bits (Kbit/s, Mbit/s) and bytes (KB/s, MB/s); the choice is remembered.
- Per-container restart policy in the start-plan editor: no, unless-stopped, always or on-failure. It applies
  live without recreating the container and is written into the template so it survives Apply. A warning badge
  marks any container left on "no".

**🎨 Design**
- Everything on the right edge lines up now: the Apps search and SHOW MORE badges, the container view toggle,
  the footer scroll arrows, and the Docker, Plugins, VM and Start-plan list rows all finish flush at the content edge.
- The settings dropdowns are the CannonadeCommand widget, with an accent-highlighted option list and no native
  browser list.
- Page and section badges use a middle size between the small badges and the main menu.
- Styled scrollbars system-wide: they follow the badge shape and the accent colour and drop their end arrows.

**⚡ Improved**
- The container view toggle stays flush right and visible even on a narrow window where the action bar overflows.
- One continuous loader with the page dimmed and blurred behind it, so the spinner is easy to see.
- Popups dim and blur the whole page including the header, the same way everywhere.
- The footer scroll arrows sit on top, side by side, tight above the bottom bar, and right aligned.

**🐛 Fixed**
- The flat badge style no longer leaves a glass sheen on grey badges anywhere.
- The plugin section headers keep their full size; only the author badges are smaller.

### 3.5.4
**Added**
- Horizontal scrolling in the Apps rows by holding the right mouse button (or Shift) and turning the wheel.

**Design**
- The Apps section headers are proper badges again, one size smaller than the main menu, with SHOW MORE as its
  own badge on the far right and a neutral info bubble that matches the rest.
- Page-title badges under the main menu bar (like "Add Container") are one size smaller than the menu, systemwide.
- The Apps category sidebar is a set of equal-width cards with clearer spacing between the sections.
- The Apps horizontal scrollbar is taller, follows the badge shape and the color mode, and drops its end arrows.

**Improved**
- The notification center and the menu now dim and blur the page behind them like every other popup.
- The container-form view toggle lines up with the form fields at any window width.

**Fixed**
- Focus no longer draws a border around the settings dropdowns or the Apps search field: it shades instead,
  per the house style (no border lines, no rings).
- The settings dropdown option list uses the CannonadeCommand surface and accent colors.
- The Apps tab no longer flashes a second, smaller spinner with a scrollbar on open: one big loader, no scrollbar.
- The Plugins tab with the tab view off: the author badges are smaller and the check-for-updates button sits at
  the top right instead of in the middle of the list.

### 3.5.3
- The two right-most header icons (notifications and menu) no longer flicker or vanish: they are re-pinned
  the instant the Connect panel re-renders, so there is no gap where they jump away.
- The settings dropdowns now match the other CannonadeCommand controls: the shape-engine radius, the same
  height, a surface fill and an accent focus ring.
- The Apps-tab search is now a collapsible button on the far right that expands into a field on click, like
  the settings search.
- The Apps-tab section headers keep the description in the info bubble and move SHOW MORE to its own badge
  flush at the right end of the row.
- The Apps-tab category sidebar is now a set of cards without separator lines that colour on hover with the
  active colour mode.
- The horizontal scrollbar on the Apps rows follows the colour mode and only appears while you hover a row;
  the stray page-level horizontal scrollbar is gone.
- The Apps tab no longer flashes a second spinner on open, and the loader is much bigger.
- The container-install window: the status check sits by the buttons instead of floating at the top, the
  pull-progress bar no longer overlaps the step cards, and the nested inner scrollbars are gone.
- The container form keeps its layout in Simple view: hidden advanced fields no longer reappear as orphan
  badges.
- The container form view toggle now lines up with the form fields instead of the window edge.
- Every popup now shares one backdrop blur so they all look the same.

### 3.5.2
- The two right-most header icons no longer flicker or disappear: each toolbar link now keys off its real
  target, so buttons that share a placeholder href stop colliding.
- Every option row in the settings (animations, density, badge shape, badge style, tile size and the rest)
  is now one unified dropdown instead of mixed segmented pills.
- The info bubbles next to each setting label sit correctly beside their label again.
- Flat vs Glass badge style is reflected live in the settings preview.
- In a color mode every settings toggle now shows its own color instead of a single flat accent.
- The Apps tab gets its own search control on the far right, matching the settings search.
- The Apps-tab badges follow the color modes like everything else.
- The Apps-tab section badges are smaller, drop the leading arrow, and move their description into an
  info bubble.
- App cards hide the transparent app background so the icons read cleanly.
- The Apps-tab sidebar is reworked into proper CannonadeCommand chips with a colored selection.
- The container-install window loses the grey title bar and the view toggle sits flush right.
- The Apps tab no longer renders a duplicated, overlapping panel when it opens.
- In every process window (update, install, create) the spinner turns into a green check when the job
  finishes instead of spinning forever.

### 3.5.1
- Footer quick-scroll arrows follow the badge shape instead of a fixed circle (the round shape was the
  fa-arrow-circle glyph, not the chip), and they no longer overlap each other.
- The Community Applications (Apps) tab goes deeper into the CannonadeCommand look: section headers become
  section badges, the search field folds into one pill, and the app cards plus their Info/Support/Install
  buttons are fully restyled.
- The "Updating Content" dialog shows only the centered loader now, with no title bar, text or buttons.
- The plugin update, container update and install windows carry the double-ring loader (the plugin update
  window previously showed no spinner at all).
- One consistent dim plus blur behind every popup: the container-create and command-palette backdrops were
  slightly sharper than the rest and now match.
- The Flat/Glass badge style covers every badge, chip, tab, button, gear, toggle and logo tile, not just the
  data pills.
- Tile size is one global control (in the General section) instead of a copy per tab.
- The share settings page no longer overflows sideways: the read/copy-settings panel stays inside the window
  with both buttons visible.
- Every popup is centered reliably, so a dialog whose content loads late (the OS update check) is no longer
  clipped off the top of the screen.
- The ShipLog changelog window corner radius is capped so it no longer renders as a lozenge at the pill shape
  (fixed in ShipLog).

### 3.5.0
- New: per-container start order. Give any container a start number in its CannonadeCommand row; within a
  start stage the plan runs lower numbers first and unnumbered containers last, and dependencies still take
  precedence over the number.
- A system-wide loader replaces the stock spinner everywhere CannonadeCommand themes a page (the tab-load
  overlay, the Community Applications "Updating Content" dialog and the plugin install/update dialog). It is a
  flat double ring that counter-rotates, its end caps follow the badge shape, and it steps through the rainbow
  palette in a colour mode.
- One backdrop behind every popup: a single, consistent dim plus blur now sits behind swal dialogs, the
  jQuery-UI menus, the notification centre and the CannonadeCommand popups.
- New: a Flat/Glass badge toggle. Glass adds a soft top sheen to every pill; flat keeps them matte.
- The Community Applications (Apps) tab now follows the CannonadeCommand look: the search field matches the
  settings search, the category sidebar reads as chips, and the app cards drop their border for a shaded,
  softly shadowed card.
- The list title bars (table headers) across the pages use the calm CannonadeCommand shade instead of the
  loud native bar.
- The Docker footer quick-scroll arrows no longer shorten the toolbar; they are raised, take the badge shape
  and follow the colour modes.
- Settings: the tile-size control now sits above the preview, the preview moved to the bottom, and resizing
  updates the preview live.
- The status island shows the grab cursor only in edit mode.
- The "Updating Content" and plugin install/update dialogs now carry the CannonadeCommand loader; the swap is
  freeze-proof (it never observes the Apps grid, which previously froze the tab).

### 3.4.3
- Fix: the main-menu search text no longer slides underneath the magnifier icon. The 3.4.2 field-height
  change had replaced the input's left padding, which the native search box uses to keep the text clear of
  the magnifier glyph; restored it (and tinted the magnifier to the CC dim tone).

### 3.4.2
- The reactive-mode toggle is now ONE toggle for every colour mode (it was duplicated per mode), placed
  directly above the "Native state colours" toggle.
- The CC settings cards now have a fixed width and no longer stretch on a wide window; the cards and the
  search icon sit flush inside the right edge instead of spilling past it.
- The notification bell and the hamburger menu can no longer be hidden (their hide toggles are gone) - they
  are integral parts of the header, and hiding them used to leave the badge without its icon.
- The full-screen tab-load spinner is now the CC loader (an accent circle with a spinning ring, hue-cycling
  in rainbow) instead of the stock red Unraid logo.
- The Docker, VM and Plugin logo tiles are now exactly the same size on every tab (they track the one shared
  size setting), and the VM logo backgrounds join the colour modes like the Docker and Plugins tabs.
- The toggles in the CC settings now follow the colour mode.
- The main-menu search: a second click on the magnifier reliably closes the box now (Escape and a click
  outside close it too); the results dropdown is styled in CC style; and the field is the same height as the
  icons.
- WILD animation mode: the bouncing menu tabs are no longer covered at the top by the header bar.

### 3.4.1
- System-wide badge engine: the badge box size metrics (data pills, tab and action badges, section
  heads) now live in ONE central place (the Tokens sheet), exactly like the colour engine and the badge
  shape engine already do. They were mirrored by hand across five sheets, so a badge could drift out of
  step; now a badge anywhere reads the same tier and a change lands everywhere at once. Pure consolidation,
  no visual change.

### 3.4.0
- Rainbow mode is now consistent across every tab. The Plugins and VMs tabs used a different, brighter palette
  and reshuffled their colours on every reload; they now share the one jewel palette and the same persisted
  rotation as the Docker, header and shares areas, so every badge lines up.
- The rainbow swatches and previews in the CC settings now default to the same jewel palette the live UI uses,
  so what you pick matches what you see.
- Reactive mode (rest grey, colour on hover, active stays lit) now works in Normal mode too, not only under
  rainbow or flag.
- The logo tiles in the Docker and Plugins tabs join the colour modes: in rainbow each tile takes its row's
  palette colour instead of one flat colour.
- The notification bell and the hamburger menu (the two rightmost header icons) now follow the colour modes
  like every other header icon.
- The orange Unraid section title bars are restyled in CC style on every page (Main, Shares, Settings, Tools,
  Users and so on), not only the Docker and Plugins tabs. The VM and Plugins section heads are rainbow aware.
- The Plugins list now spans the full window width when the tab view is off (it was capped to the left half).
- The CC settings cards and search field close flush with the right edge.
- The combined "Settings and Tools tabs" section in the CC settings is split into two separate tabs, and the
  CC settings tab order now strictly and live follows your main menu order.
- VM RAM can now be raised above the VM's current maximum; the extra headroom applies on the next VM start.
- The CPU, RAM and bandwidth popups on the VM tab now open right at their gear instead of centred in the window.
- The Docker "Einfache Ansicht" toggle no longer overlaps the native scroll arrows, and those arrows are
  recoloured into the CC accent.
- WILD animation mode no longer clips the bouncing menu tabs at the top.
- The tab-load spinner is unified with the update-window spinner, and in rainbow it changes colour each turn.
- The VMs main tab now opens on the first click.

### 3.3.0
- VM tab: full per-VM resource control, matched exactly to the Docker tab. CPU, RAM and bandwidth each get
  their own badge with a gear behind it, coloured per kind. The CPU editor has the same graphical core-picker
  the Docker tab uses (one box per physical core, Intel P and E cores tagged), plus a CPU cap; RAM sets the
  balloon size; bandwidth caps upload and download and the badge shows the live throughput while a VM runs.
  The CPU pin and cap are applied with virsh and re-asserted every tick, so an Unraid VM-form Apply can no
  longer silently drop the cap; bandwidth is policed host-side because this kernel lacks the qdiscs libvirt
  would otherwise need.
- VM tab: live vDisk grow. A gear on the vDisks badge opens a resize editor; the disk grows live via
  blockresize while the VM runs, or via qemu-img while it is off. It is grow-only and refuses any size it
  cannot verify as larger, so a disk can never be truncated.
- The CPU, RAM and bandwidth limit editors are now identical between the Docker and VM tabs: the same dark
  surface, radius, elevation, header with a close button and controls. The lighter inner cards behind the
  fields are gone, so an editor reads as one flat, lit surface.
- Speed: the reskin now paints as soon as the rows appear instead of after a fixed pause, so switching tabs no
  longer flashes the plain Unraid list before the badges and gears land.
- Header: the notification bell's unread indicator is a small corner dot again instead of a blob that
  half-covered the bell.
- Table title bars: every list's column-header row is now in the CannonadeCommand style (quiet tracked
  small-caps on a subtle bar), consistent across pages and both themes.
- The badge-shape setting is now system-wide: pill, rounded, square or circle also drives the gears, the
  toggles and their knobs, and the colour swatches, not just the badges.
- Settings: the server-name font list is sorted alphabetically, the old ugly faces are gone, and a curated set
  of Google fonts (Montserrat, Poppins, Oswald, Bebas Neue, Playfair Display and more) was added; they load on
  demand and render for everyone. The dead Help-icon toggle was removed (the Help button is long gone), and the
  density row is aligned like every other row.
- Animations are now a three-way choice: off, normal, or wild. Wild adds very present motion (the main-menu
  tabs hop on hover, pills and gears spring, popovers bounce in, the wordmark wobbles).
- Finish: a lit elevation and a soft entrance on the popovers; a convex sheen and tracked small-caps on every
  badge; tabular figures so live numbers do not jitter the columns; a jewel-toned rainbow palette; crisp line
  gears in place of the emoji cog; a soft focus ring; an in-place copy flash; and a state glyph on the running,
  paused and stopped badges so state reads without relying on colour alone.
### 3.2.1
- Required container fields: the red "required" dot is shown consistently on every required field now, including
  dropdown fields (e.g. "Behind reverse proxy"), which previously still showed the native asterisk.
- Status badge: the running loader is a spinning update-arrow now (the same spinner Unraid shows on a
  container's logo while it updates) instead of the plain 3-dot loader, still turning into a filled green check
  when the run finishes.
- Container install / recreate output window ("Add container"): fully reworked from real measurements. A stray
  accent square under the title (a leftover native heading streamed back into the window) is gone; long log
  lines (image URLs, volume paths) wrap instead of forcing a horizontal scrollbar; a long pull log scrolls
  inside its own card instead of scrolling the whole window; and the same spinning status badge (green check
  when done) now shows while the install or recreate runs.
- Loading animation: it only appears where a process actually runs now. The System Information window no longer
  shows a spinner (its content sits in a plain fieldset, which was mistaken for a running stream).
### 3.2.0
- Floating windows (system information, confirmations, changelog): the window surface was as dark as the dimmed
  backdrop behind it, so a dialog barely stood out. Every dialog frame now sits on the lighter card surface
  (#242424) and clearly lifts off the backdrop; the raw streaming log keeps its deep terminal inset.
- Container update window: no loading animation showed while an update ran, because the German title
  ("... wird aktualisiert") never matched the English "in progress" the loader looked for. The running state is
  now detected from the localized progress verbs and from the live streaming log, so the 3-dot loader shows
  during the run and turns into a filled green status badge when it finishes. The status badge sits directly to
  the LEFT of the buttons, with the same gap as between the buttons.
- Container install window ("Add container"): matched exactly to the update window now (same lighter surface,
  same soft shadow and radius, no hairline ring, step cards on the window surface).
- ShipLog changelog window: stray border lines on the version blocks are removed (CC never draws lines, it
  separates by shade).
- Add-container form: the Categories field is the same height as the other value fields now (it was slightly
  taller and misaligned).
- Settings action buttons (Apply / Done / Save): they used to each take a different rainbow colour, which read
  as arbitrary. They are one uniform accent now, so the button row is consistent.
- Server-name editor: many more font choices (about 70 now); the open font list is darker.
- CannonadeCommand settings: the hex colour field is lighter (the standard chip surface), so it clearly reads
  as the same size box as the colour swatches next to it.
- Density control: the "(global)" note moved out of the label into an (i) bubble that explains it, and the
  switches sit to the LEFT of the label now.
- VM tab: the bottom action buttons, the per-row action icons and the info badges all follow the colour mode
  correctly in every mode now (accent, full rainbow, and reactive, where they rest grey and colour on hover),
  and they repaint on a colour-mode change instead of keeping stale colours.
- Users page: the user tiles are proper CannonadeCommand tiles now (the avatar is an accent icon badge that
  follows the colour and shape engine, the name below it), with more spacing; the page buttons are accent pills
  instead of the native orange outline.
- Toggles: the shape engine turned the track AND the knob into rounded squares, so a toggle read as a boxy
  block instead of a switch. Toggles are always a pill track with a round knob now (badges still follow the
  shape setting).
- Settings subtabs (Mover, TRIM, SMB Extras): the schedule rows are native lists with a stray info-icon element
  that the grid scattered (label pushed far right, the field wrapping to the far left). Those rows line up with
  the other rows now while keeping the native alignment.
### 3.1.1
- Header Help ("?") button removal did not take on the live install: the hide rule was out-specified by the base
  nav-item rule, so the button stayed visible. It is properly hidden now.
### 3.1.0
- Boot device SMB Security: the two "copy settings" dropdown checklists finally open. The jQuery dropdownchecklist
  sizes its drop panel once at init, and it initialised while the reka tab was still hidden (zero width), so the
  panel collapsed to nothing. It is now re-initialised against the visible selector when the tab is shown. The
  "read settings from" selector no longer overflows the button next to it.
- The SMB "copy settings" checklist is a full CannonadeCommand dropdown now, identical to the other CC dropdowns:
  the native square checkboxes are gone, each entry is a rounded chip that lights up in its own palette colour when
  selected, and the panel matches the CC dropdowns exactly (same width, padding, row spacing and height). The close
  row is a muted footer. Select, close and re-open all verified against the real widget.
- Boot Parameters: every toggle is a full-size CannonadeCommand pill now (the reka editor drew them at a tiny
  "narrow" size), and the clickable parameter-code chips (the kernel argument each option inserts) rotate through
  the palette like every other button instead of staying flat grey.
- Notification centre: the tabs and type filters used to all show the same single accent, because the drawer mounts
  after the palette paint ran. The paint now re-runs when the drawer opens, so every tab and filter gets its own
  rotating colour again. The bulk delete glyph is white (was red), and the delete button rotates with the palette
  like the archive button (it was a weak faint-red before); the "armed" confirm state keeps its red.
- Account menu (Manage License / Check for Updates / Account / Settings) is CannonadeCommand-styled with rotating
  item hover. The "Manage License" description folds onto a click (i) help bubble instead of a paragraph, and the
  two external-link glyphs on the account items are removed.
- Floating help bubbles now render above the account menu and the notification drawer (both live in a very high
  z-index layer that used to cover the bubble).
- Header Help ("?") button removed: with all inline help moved into (i) bubbles system-wide it had nothing left to
  toggle.
- Header notification and burger icons are individually draggable in arrange mode and no longer jump or drag their
  neighbours when the window is resized; the status-island chips arrange freely across the header with their rows
  staying fixed.
- Boot device: all five sub-tabs (Boot Device, Boot Device Settings, SMB Security, Boot Parameters, Boot Mode) are
  CannonadeCommand-styled and aligned, section headings are badges, and the hairline borders are gone. The disk
  tables end flush with the status island and their hover bars follow the badge shape.
### 3.0.1
- Help button: removed the misleading "This page has no inline help" toast. On pages like the Docker list the
  native help blocks live in a hidden (display:none) template container, so there is genuinely nothing to show,
  and on Tools/Settings pages CannonadeCommand already moved the help into the (i) info bubbles. The toast fired on
  exactly those pages and only annoyed. Help now behaves like native: it shows help where the page actually has it.
### 3.0.0
- Community Applications installs are finally CannonadeCommand-styled. CA opens the container template at
  /Apps/AddContainer (not /Docker/AddContainer), where CC's script hook did not load, so the add form AND the
  install-output window came up native/flat. The hook and the form/output detection now cover /(Docker|Apps)/, so
  the CC form styling and the floating output window apply on the CA path too.
- Docker allocations ("Docker-Zuweisungen"): new sort control (by container name A-Z, or by IP) above the list.
- Docker allocations: aligned with the form's value column instead of sitting far to the left, and the rows now
  fill the width so the four columns (name / network / IP / ports) spread evenly instead of huddling at the left.
- Notifications drawer: each message is a proper card now (raised surface, rounded, spaced) instead of a plain
  line-separated row, and the top tabs/buttons share one consistent height and radius.
### 2.99.0
- Removed the Docker multiselect (#S7) and the container note/tag (#S8) features again (user set them aside).
- "Add Container" / template form no longer stays completely native: the CC styling (dl grids, CC dropdowns, colon-
  stripped labels) failed when the form was injected into #canvas AFTER boot()'s one-shot check. A scoped re-detection
  watcher now restyles it whenever the form (or the run OUTPUT) appears, however the page was reached.
- Container-UPDATE window (the ".sweet-alert" progress popup) is finally restyled: in this Unraid build it lacks the
  "nchan" class, so every nchan-scoped fix missed it. CC now also matches ".sweet-alert:has(pre)" and stamps the class,
  so the title carries NO status text, the loader sits bottom-left (3 dots -> green circle-with-check), the empty grey
  bar is hidden, and the title is a FULL-WIDTH bar.
- Inline "Add Container" output is a real, centered window/card again with a full-width title bar (consistent with the
  update window).
- Action icons: 3 per row; the "…" expander sits as the 4th icon of row 2; clicking it hides the "…" and fades in the
  remaining icons (3 per row); moving the mouse off the cluster auto-collapses it.
- Status island: entering arrange mode no longer reflows all chips (v2.94's "wider drop zones" widened the island and
  forced rows to full width). Chips stay in place now and just wiggle.
- Settings subtabs (Docker, VM Manager, Power mode, ...): the section STATUS dot follows the badge-shape setting and the
  colour modes; the auto-centered toggle controls are pinned left so toggles, fields and values line up like native;
  native radio buttons are CC-styled; the VM-Manager "Remove" beside the VirtIO-ISO dropdown becomes a trash icon like
  the Plugins tab.
- CC settings: the "Display - header" card is merged into the Theming card; the native-settings "Open" button is now
  right-aligned.
### 2.98.0
- Bugfix pass (changelog QA, verified live):
- #S8 The container note/tag could not be opened by clicking - the click instead triggered the row's
  action flash (the tag sits in the same row). The tag and multiselect box now capture their own clicks;
  the note editor opens again.
- Docker gears: in full rainbow mode a gear again carried the accent instead of its CPU/RAM/BW child
  colour on hover - now its own child colour in EVERY colour mode.
- Status island: fixed a rare case where temperature chips and chip arranging/dragging silently failed on
  pages without a global helper variable (undeclared loop variable under "use strict").
- Tool pages: the native help button falsely reported "no inline help" even though CC had moved the texts
  into the (i) bubbles - now it only reports that when there really is no help.
- Border lines (CC rule "no lines"): removed the 1px row line on tool tables and the 1px border of the
  input fields in the popup windows (dark surface only now).
- Light theme: the hint toast now also gets the light surface in the azure theme (Theme--azure).
### 2.97.0
- Light theme (#S9, first pass): CannonadeCommand is dark-first; solid dark badges/cards read well on a
  light background too, but elements with a weak/transparent surface now get a light surface + dark text
  in the white/azure Unraid theme so nothing disappears.
### 2.96.0
- New #S7: Docker multiselect - a selection checkbox on the left of each container; when any are ticked, a
  batch bar appears at the bottom (start/stop/restart/pause for all selected).
- New #S8: container notes/tags - a small note badge per container (click to edit), stays saved.
- "Add/update container" window (inline output): now like the other update window - dark surface, a
  centered pill title instead of an orange full-width bar, borderless step cards, buttons in colour mode.
### 2.95.0
- Edit container: "Current Docker allocations" aligned like native again (constrained + centered, not
  full-width against the left edge); the category dropdown now sits flush on the same edge/width as the
  other fields.
### 2.94.0
- Arrange (rebuild): no more dedicated lock - CannonadeCommand uses Unraid's own arrange/lock icon (which
  otherwise only appears on the Dashboard) and shows it persistently on ALL tabs; one click activates
  arrange mode (menu tabs + island chips wiggle + immediately movable).
- Status island: much larger arrange area (big drop zones) for easier moving.
- CannonadeCommand settings: all toggles now follow the colour mode; the favourites hint sits in an (i)
  bubble instead of inline; the "Native display page" card now has text + (i) bubble + a short "Open"
  button side by side; many more fonts for the server name.
- Tool/settings subpages: native toggle switches, multiselect lists and checkboxes in CC style, borders
  removed, orange hint cards without borders, section headings as accent badges.
### 2.93.0
- Tool/settings subpages: label and value sit COMPACTLY side by side again (like native) instead of spread
  across the full width - fixes "completely misplaced" on Date/Time, Language and others.
- CannonadeCommand settings: the hex field has no border line and is exactly as tall as the colour fields;
  the reset button is now exactly one colour-field cell in size.
- Edit container: the field-label badges are plain text again (consistent with the other pages).
- Native checkboxes on tool pages in CC style (dark, accent check, borderless).
### 2.92.0
- New: command palette with Ctrl/Cmd+K - quickly search and jump to any page (and a few CC actions), fully
  keyboard-operable (arrows/Enter/Esc).
- Arrange lock: round icon corrected (was too wide).
### 2.91.0
- Arrange via lock (instead of hold): a lock icon (always visible, top right) unlocks arranging. Click
  -&gt; the menu tabs and island chips wiggle and can be moved IMMEDIATELY; clicking again (or Esc) locks
  again and saves the arrangement. No more fiddly press-and-hold; while locked, tabs/chips navigate
  normally.
### 2.90.0
- Display settings: the three header colour fields (text/secondary text/background) now have a real
  colour-picker field (swatch) next to the hex field, synced both ways.
- Floating window: the title badge now shows NO status text and no loader anymore. The loading animation
  sits bottom left next to the buttons (3 dots, no text) and turns into a green circle-with-check when done.
- Empty grey step cards (the bar above the buttons) are hidden more reliably; the bottom buttons are now
  arranged uniformly (primary button on the right) like in the template window.
### 2.89.0
- Docker gears in reactive colour mode: on hovering a row all gears glowed orange (accent) instead of their
  own CPU/RAM/BW colour. Now each gear carries its child colour on hover too.

### 2.88.0
- Alignment (finally fundamental): server name and content now align flush to the main menu bar on EVERY
  page - even on pages without their own CannonadeCommand section (e.g. the settings overview) that slipped
  through before. The brand is additionally placed exactly at the menu edge by measurement.

### 2.87.0
- Status island CPU (FINALLY): the cause was that Unraid's CPU value runs over a GraphQL WEBSOCKET that
  reverse proxies (e.g. the *.lol tunnel) do not pass through (handshake 200 instead of 101) - so the chip
  stayed empty. CannonadeCommand now reads CPU load via its OWN engine over normal HTTP (proc/stat delta) -
  proxy-safe, on every page. First shows 0%, then live.
- Display/tool pages: description texts now stay in the (i) bubble EVEN when you press the native help
  button (which otherwise re-showed the texts via jQuery).

### 2.86.0
- Template update window ("Update container"): now looks like the CA update window - dark surface, a
  centered pill title badge instead of an orange full-width bar, step cards without borders, section badges
  as accent pills, the blue status box neutralized. (Different window type - CreateDocker iframe - hence
  untouched until now.)
- Floating window: the useless light-grey bar above the buttons is gone (empty/legend-only step cards are
  now hidden reliably).
- Display/tool pages: ALL description texts now land in the (i) info bubble (some stayed inline before when
  no label was found - now falls back to the value column).

### 2.85.0
- Help icon (FINALLY the root): the docked user profile (bell/menu) sat as an invisible surface OVER the
  help icon and swallowed the real mouse click (a synthetic test click went through, which is why it seemed
  to "work"). The dock surface is now click-through; only bell + menu capture clicks. Plus a reliable
  fallback handler. The help click now works reliably on every page.
- Status island CPU: Unraid 7.3 removed the old CPU channel - CannonadeCommand now reads CPU load from
  Unraid's GraphQL metrics (like the native Dashboard). The CPU chip shows percentages again instead of "--".
- Status island temperature: on this server the system temperature plugin had lost its sensor assignment
  (CPU/MB labels missing) - restored, CPU and mainboard temperature are shown again.
- CannonadeCommand settings: colour fields, hex field and reset are now a uniform row of cells (each cell
  the same size; the hex field takes two cells, so one or two fewer colour fields in that row) - identical
  in ALL cards. The animations toggle now sits in the Theming card (no separate almost-empty card).

### 2.84.0
- Floating window (container update): the step cards AGAIN have NO border lines - the card look comes only
  from an offset surface + shadow (CC style never has border lines). Regression from 2.81.0 fixed.
- The top title badge is again clearly larger than the section badges (clear size hierarchy).
- The loading animation no longer sits at the top of the badge but bottom left next to the close button -
  as a clean, modern 3-dot pulse animation in the colour-mode colour.

### 2.83.0
- Accessibility: the CannonadeCommand dropdowns can now be operated entirely by keyboard (open with
  Enter/Space/Arrow-down, select with arrow keys, close with Esc) and report roles/states to screen
  readers (listbox/option, aria-expanded/aria-selected).
- After an update a short hint toast greets you with the new version number (only after real updates, not
  on the first install).

### 2.82.0
- CannonadeCommand settings: all colour fields, the hex field and the reset button of a colour row are now
  exactly the same height system-wide (28px) - including the previously smaller top row.
- New "Animations" toggle (General, on by default): smooth transitions/motion across the entire interface.
  ON also overrides the system "reduce motion" setting; OFF stills everything. Plus subtle new motions
  (fade-in of the status island/brand, hover lift of the cards).

### 2.81.0
- Docker page: the CPU/RAM/BW gears were all orange in rainbow mode - now each gear carries its badge's own
  palette colour (CPU/RAM/bandwidth).
- Dropdown lists: in reactive colour mode the list entries now rest neutral and only light up in their
  colour on hover (previously coloured permanently).
- CannonadeCommand settings: the favourites section can only be enabled when Unraid's own favourites
  feature is active; otherwise the toggle is disabled and a hint explains why.
- Floating window: the scrollbar no longer sits right at the edge (moved slightly inward), the sections
  (step cards) have an offset card look again, and all buttons/badges follow the colour mode.
- Help icon: when a page has no inline help, a short hint toast now appears instead of seemingly "nothing
  happening" (the help itself worked but had nothing to show on some pages).
- Header icons (bell/menu): now sit exactly flush with the status island (a few pixels to the left).

### 2.80.0
- Section badges (e.g. "ARRAY DEVICES"): with the "Boxed" display width active on wide screens they now
  align flush left with the main menu bar again (the centered content is pulled left-flush to the
  full-width menu).
- Help icon: the click now reliably triggers the native help (robust handler so the click is not swallowed).

### 2.79.0
- Dropdown lists (tools/settings): the open button now colours ONLY on hover (no longer permanently); the
  list entries in the open panel each have their own palette colour in rainbow mode.
- Floating windows (container update, system info, feedback): a consistent dark surface throughout
  (0f0f0f) - no lighter header/footer bar anymore.
- Docker page: the status dot under the container name is no longer a toggle - hovering it shows the current
  status, a click makes the action icons flash. The CPU/RAM/BW gears are now fully integrated into the
  colour modes in reactive mode too.
- CannonadeCommand settings: the favourites toggle on the display page now takes effect (Unraid's favourites
  setting is coupled with CannonadeCommand's "Hide favourites"). The search badge follows the colour mode.
- Main menu bar: the two docked icons (bell, menu) sit flush with the other icons again.
- Status island: chip arranging by dragging is smoother (shorter hold time), larger drop zones, and the
  chips wiggle in arrange mode.

### 2.78.0
- Statusinsel: Die Chips lassen sich jetzt per Ziehen (kurz gedrueckt halten, dann ziehen) frei auf DREI Zeilen
  anordnen; die Anordnung wird gespeichert. Ein Klick auf einen Chip springt auf die passende Seite (Array/
  Fuellstand -> Start, Container -> Docker, RAM/CPU/Temperatur -> Uebersicht).
- Bewegungsreduzierung: Ist im Betriebssystem "Bewegung reduzieren" aktiv, verzichtet CannonadeCommand auf
  Wackel-/Puls-Animationen und Uebergaenge.

### 2.77.0
- Werkzeug-/Einstellungen-Subseiten: Klickt man das Hilfe-Symbol in der Menueleiste, werden die einge-
  blendeten Hilfetexte jetzt sauber ueber die volle Breite und im CannonadeCommand-Note-Stil angezeigt
  (statt in eine Rasterspalte gequetscht).

### 2.76.0
- Docker-Seite: Der Ansichts-Umschalter (Einfach/Erweitert) sitzt wieder in der unteren Leiste. Der Laeuft/
  Gestoppt-Punkt sitzt jetzt UNTER dem Container-Namen und ist im reaktiven Modus integriert (ruht grau,
  faerbt sich beim Zeilen-Hover). Ein Klick auf den Container-NAMEN oeffnet nicht mehr die Vorlage, sondern
  laesst die Aktions-Icons aufblitzen (wie der Klick aufs Logo). Die CPU-/RAM-/BW-Zahnraeder folgen dem Farbmodus.
- Schwebefenster: Die hellen Kopf-/Fussleisten sind jetzt auch im Container-Update-Fenster (tiefere Wrapper)
  UND in den iframe-Fenstern (Systeminformation, Feedback) durchgehend dunkel; das Feedback-Fenster ist im
  CannonadeCommand-Stil und schmaler.
- Werkzeug-/Einstellungen-Subseiten: Die Dropdown-Listen wechseln im Regenbogen-Modus jetzt pro Zeile die Farbe
  (sonst Akzentfarbe). Beschriftung und Feld/Toggle sitzen jetzt sauber auf einer Ebene. Die Ja/Nein-Toggles
  (z. B. Banner anzeigen, Favoriten) wirken jetzt LIVE (sie speichern die Aenderung und laden neu).
- Startseite: Die Fuellstandsbalken blinken nicht mehr, wenn "Zustandsanzeigen nativ faerben" an ist (sie
  werden synchron beim Neuaufbau der Tabelle eingefaerbt).
- Hauptmenueleiste: Die beiden rechten Icons (Glocke, Menue) haben jetzt auch die neue groessere Groesse.
- CannonadeCommand-Einstellungen: "Kopf-Farben ans Thema koppeln" ist standardmaessig an. Der Reset-Knopf der
  Regenbogen-/Flaggenfarben ist jetzt ein Badge. Das Suchfeld folgt der Badge-Form und schliesst beim Klick daneben.
- Statusinsel: Der Container-Chip zeigt jetzt auch die Anzahl gestoppter Container (laufend / gestoppt). Aktivierte
  Chips ohne aktuelle Daten (Fuellstand, CPU-Last) erscheinen jetzt mit Platzhalter, statt zu verschwinden.

### 2.75.0
- Docker-Seite: Der Laeuft/Gestoppt-Status wird jetzt tatsaechlich als kleiner Farb-Punkt rechts neben dem
  Container-Namen angezeigt (in 2.74.0 blieb noch das Text-Badge stehen, weil der Status-Ticker es neu
  aufbaute - der Punkt-Look haengt jetzt am Zeilen-Container und ueberlebt den Neuaufbau).
- Werkzeug-/Einstellungen-Subseiten: Die Dropdown-Listen sind jetzt im CannonadeCommand-Stil (schwebendes
  Auswahl-Panel mit Chips, ausgewaehlt/ueberfahren in Akzentfarbe) statt der nativen Betriebssystem-Liste.
- Anzeige-Einstellungen: Die Info-Bubbles, die Unraid nur auf Englisch liefert (das deutsche Sprachpaket
  uebersetzt einige Hilfetexte nicht), erscheinen jetzt auf Deutsch.

### 2.74.0
- Zustands- und Fuellstandsanzeigen auf der Startseite: Die Disk-Zustandspunkte folgen jetzt dem Farbmodus und
  sind in den reaktiven Modus aufgenommen (ruhen grau, nehmen beim Ueberfahren der Zeile die Palettenfarbe an);
  die Fuellbalken ebenso. Bei "Zustandsanzeigen nativ faerben" AN zeigen die Balken wieder gruen/gelb/rot nach
  Fuellgrad - und eine fast leere Platte wird NICHT mehr faelschlich mit rotem Balken dargestellt (der Frei-
  Balken folgt jetzt dem Belegt-Zustand). Die Umfaerbung laeuft rein ueber CSS, damit nichts mehr flackert.
- VM-Liste: Das VM-Logo / der Icon-Hintergrund ist jetzt in den reaktiven Farbmodus integriert.
- Docker-Seite: Der Laeuft/Gestoppt-Status ist ein kleiner Farb-Punkt rechts neben dem Container-Namen (wie die
  Disk-Zustandspunkte) statt eines Text-Badges - einfaerbbar wie die Disk-Punkte, Form nach Badge-Einstellung.
  Der Einfach/Erweitert-Umschalter sitzt jetzt oben rechts in der Ecke.
- Schwebefenster (Container-Update / Plugin-Changelog): Titel-Badge und Buttons haben wieder die Standard-
  Groesse (nicht mehr uebergross); Kopf- und Fussleiste sind durchgehend dunkel.
- Werkzeug-/Einstellungen-Subseiten: Die (i)-Info-Symbole sitzen jetzt sauber auf der Textlinie; die Toggles
  folgen der Badge-Form (Pille/abgerundet/eckig).
- Badge-Groessen systemweit vereinheitlicht: Die Hauptmenue-Badges sind die groesste Stufe (Icons daneben
  gleich hoch); die Abschnitts- und Titelbadges sind einheitlich eine Stufe kleiner - Startseite, Einstellungen
  und alle Subseiten gleich.
- CannonadeCommand-Einstellungen: Der Link zu den nativen Anzeige-Einstellungen ist ein CC-Akzent-Button; die
  Dichte-Einstellung ist in die Theming-Karte gewandert; das Suchfeld sitzt oben rechts als aufklappbarer
  Symbol-Badge; die UI-/Engine-Version steht ganz unten.

### 2.73.0
- Die VM-Liste ist jetzt in den REAKTIVEN Farbmodus integriert: bei aktivem reaktivem Regenbogen-/Flaggen-
  Modus ruhen die Badges grau und nehmen die Palettenfarbe erst beim Ueberfahren der Zeile an.

### 2.72.0
- Weitere Farbmodus-/Subseiten-Nachbesserungen:
- Button-Gruppen rotieren jetzt nach VISUELLER Zeile durch die Palette (auch wenn die Buttons in
  verschiedenen Containern liegen), sodass nebeneinanderstehende Buttons zuverlaessig unterschiedliche
  Farben haben.
- Die (i)-Info-Symbole sitzen jetzt zuverlaessig an ihrer Beschriftung (vorher lagen sie auf manchen
  Subseiten am linken Rand daneben, wenn der native Hilfetext direkt im Formular stand).
- Docker-Einstellungsseite: der Laeuft-/Gestoppt-Status ist jetzt ein kleiner Farb-Punkt im Titel-Badge
  (wie die Zustandspunkte bei den Datentraegern) statt farbigem Text.

### 2.71.0
- Nachbesserungen an den Farbmodi:
- Im Regenbogen-Modus bekommen jetzt nebeneinanderstehende Buttons (z. B. auf den Werkzeug-/Einstellungen-
  Subseiten und im Freigaben-Tab) sowie die Schalter jeweils UNTERSCHIEDLICHE Palettenfarben statt einer
  Einheitsfarbe - sie rotieren durch die Palette.
- Die nativen Schalter auf den Einstellungen-Subseiten (z. B. "Docker aktivieren") haben jetzt die
  CannonadeCommand-Pillen-Form und folgen dem Farbmodus.
- Auslastungsbalken und diese Elemente werden jetzt auch dann eingefaerbt, wenn die Seite ihren Inhalt erst
  nachlaedt (ein Beobachter faerbt spaet gerenderte Balken/Buttons nach).

### 2.70.0
- Konsistenz-Runde (Teil 4):
- Zustandsanzeige-Umfang: Das Update-Badge auf der Docker-Seite und die Badges in der Status-Spalte des
  Plugin-Tabs gehoeren jetzt zur Zustandsanzeige - bei "Zustandsanzeigen nativ faerben" AUS folgen sie dem
  Farbmodus, AN bleiben sie in ihrer nativen Signalfarbe (gruen/gelb).
- Das Kategorien-Feld im Docker-Formular fuellt jetzt die Wertespalte und sitzt buendig wie die anderen Felder.

### 2.69.0
- Konsistenz-Runde (Teil 3) - native Werkzeug-/Einstellungen-Subseiten:
- Die Ueberschrift oben auf jeder Werkzeug-/Einstellungen-Subseite ist jetzt ein Badge statt eines grauen
  Balkens.
- Die nativen Infotexte (die beim Anklicken einer Einstellung erscheinen) sitzen jetzt hinter einem
  kleinen (i)-Symbol an der Beschriftung und erscheinen als CannonadeCommand-Sprechblase beim Ueberfahren.
- Einstellungen mit nur Ja/Nein bekommen jetzt einen Schalter statt einer Auswahlliste.
- Nachtrag: die Auslastungs-/Fuellstandsbalken folgen jetzt zuverlaessig dem Farbmodus (die Loesung
  greift auch fuer spaeter nachgeladene Balken).

### 2.68.0
- Konsistenz-Runde (Teil 2):
- Auslastungs-/Fuellstandsbalken folgen jetzt dem Farbmodus, wenn der Schalter "Zustandsanzeigen nativ
  faerben" AUS ist (AN = weiterhin nativ gruen/gelb/rot je nach Fuellstand).
- System-Stats: die Steuerung unter den Graphen sitzt jetzt als aufgeraeumte Zeile, und der
  Zuruecksetzen-Knopf sitzt rechts und folgt dem Farbmodus.
- Kopfbereich-Karte: die nativen Kopf-Farben liegen jetzt auf Unraids Anzeige-Seite (im
  CannonadeCommand-Stil), die Karte hat nur noch den Schnellzugriff; NEU: ein Schalter, der die
  Kopf-Farben automatisch an Unraids Farbschema koppelt (dunkles Thema: dunkler Hintergrund + helle
  Schrift; helles Thema umgekehrt).
- Auf den Werkzeug- und Einstellungen-Subseiten werden die Doppelpunkte hinter den Beschriftungen entfernt.

### 2.67.0
- Konsistenz-Runde quer durch die Tabs (Teil 1):
- Farbwaehl-Zeile ueberall gleich: das Hex-Feld sitzt jetzt als rechte Zelle direkt neben den Farbfeldern
  und die Zeile fuellt sich ganz aus, wie die Regenbogen-Felder mit ihrem Reset.
- Aktions-Buttons folgen jetzt dem Farbmodus: die Buttons im Freigaben-Tab und auf den Werkzeug- und
  Einstellungen-Subseiten nehmen die Regenbogen-/Flaggenfarbe an, wenn ein Farbmodus aktiv ist (sonst den Akzent).
- VM-Tab: alle Badges (auch Snapshots/Beschreibung/Grafik) und der Autostart-Schalter folgen jetzt dem Farbmodus.
- VM-Nutzungsstatistiken: der VM-Name ist jetzt ein Badge, und die Ansicht flackert beim Aktualisieren nicht
  mehr kurz ins native Design zurueck (Neu-Auszeichnung laeuft jetzt vor dem Neuzeichnen).
- Docker-Zuweisungen: die Liste nutzt die volle Breite mit gleichmaessig verteilten Spalten und hat jetzt
  abwechselnde Zeilenfarben, damit sie leichter zu lesen ist.
- Das Vorlagen-Dropdown auf der Docker-Seite schliesst nicht mehr sofort, wenn man in der Liste scrollt.

### 2.66.4
- Die streamenden Schwebefenster (Plugin-Installation/-Update und Container-Update) sehen jetzt alle
  gleich aus: Der Titel-Badge oben ist einheitlich breit und prominent und exakt so hoch wie die
  Aktions-Buttons unten (46px). Die Schritt-Karten im Container-Update-Fenster hatten einen leicht
  helleren Hintergrund (#1c1c1c) als das Fenster - das wirkte oben und unten wie ein heller Balken;
  sie sind jetzt auf das Fenster-Dunkel (#161616) gesetzt, sodass das ganze Fenster eine durchgehend
  dunkle Flaeche ist.

### 2.66.3
- Die Farbtrennungs-Migration bereinigt jetzt AUCH den Engine-seitigen Einstellungs-Spiegel. CC
  synchronisiert alle Farb-/Modus-Einstellungen ueber die Engine zwischen Browsern; die alten
  Flaggenfarben steckten also nicht nur im Browser, sondern auch in diesem Spiegel und wurden beim
  naechsten Laden immer wieder zurueckgespielt. Beim Laden der Einstellungen werden die Flaggenfarben
  jetzt im Spiegel in den Flaggen-Speicher verschoben und aus dem Regenbogen-Speicher entfernt und die
  bereinigte Konfiguration wird zurueckgeschrieben - sodass die Regenbogen-Farbfelder dauerhaft sauber
  bleiben. Deckt auch Installationen ab, die 2.66.1 oder 2.66.2 schon eingespielt hatten.

### 2.66.2
- Die in 2.66.1 eingefuehrte Migration der Farbtrennung laeuft jetzt zuverlaessig: Sie zieht die
  Flaggenfarben aus dem alten gemeinsamen Speicher DIREKT in den neuen Flaggen-Speicher (die Werte sind
  identisch, es ist keine Flaggen-Datenbank noetig) und setzt die Regenbogen-Palette auf den Standard
  zurueck. Sie laeuft schon beim Laden der Einstellungen, bevor irgendetwas gezeichnet wird, sodass die
  Regenbogen-Farbfelder auf einer aktualisierten Installation nicht mehr die Flaggenfarben zeigen.

### 2.66.1
- Nachtrag zur Farbtrennung: Auf einer FRISCH aktualisierten Installation, auf der vorher schon der
  Flaggen-Modus aktiv war, steckten die Flaggenfarben noch im gemeinsamen alten Speicher und faerbten die
  Regenbogen-Farbfelder weiter ein. Beim Oeffnen der Einstellungen laeuft jetzt eine einmalige Migration:
  Sie legt die Flaggenpalette in ihren eigenen Speicher und setzt die Regenbogen-Palette auf den sauberen
  Standard zurueck. Danach sind Regenbogen und Flagge auch auf Altinstallationen vollstaendig getrennt.

### 2.66.0
- Die Badge-Einstellungskarte ist komplett neu geordnet: Farbfeld + Regler, darunter die Preset-Felder mit
  dem Hex-Feld rechts daneben, dann die drei Regenbogen-Schalter (Modus, reaktiv, Farbrotation) mit den
  Regenbogen-Farbfeldern (ohne Ueberschrift, der Reset ist jetzt gleich gross wie ein Farbfeld), danach der
  Flaggen-Modus - die Laenderauswahl ist jetzt ein klarer Button ohne Mini-Pfeil, die Laenderliste bleibt
  scrollbar und wird nicht mehr vom Kartenrand abgeschnitten - mit reaktivem Flaggen-Modus und acht
  Flaggenfarben samt Reset, dann die Badge-Form (eine Zeile, nach Rundung sortiert), die Zustandsanzeigen und
  zuletzt eine groessere Vorschau mit acht Badges. Die Paletten-Presets sind entfernt.
- Regenbogen und Flagge haben jetzt getrennte Farbspeicher. Der Flaggen-Modus faerbt die Regenbogen-Farbfelder
  nicht mehr ein, und die Flaggenfarben tauchen nicht mehr auf der Docker-Seite (oder anderswo) auf, wenn der
  Flaggen-Modus gar nicht aktiv ist. Jeder Farb-Leser (Menueleiste, Freigaben, Plugins, Einstellungen, VMs,
  Docker) waehlt sauber ENTWEDER die Flaggen- ODER die Regenbogen-Palette, nie beide vermischt.

### 2.65.0
- Das Plugin-Install- und Container-Update-Fenster ist aufgeraeumt: die grellgruene "Ball-Fall"-Ladeanimation
  ist weg, stattdessen dreht sich ein cleaner moderner Ring-Spinner LINKS am Titel-Badge, und der Badge wird
  ausgegraut solange der Vorgang laeuft (danach faerbt er sich wieder). Die leeren grauen Fieldset-Balken oben
  und unten (Unraids Reste) werden ausgeblendet - das Fenster ist jetzt durchgehend dunkel und ruhig.

### 2.64.2
- #14 Wenn ein Container angelegt/angewendet wird, ist die Ausgabe (docker-run-Befehl + Ergebnis) jetzt ein
  schwebendes Fenster wie das Container-Update-Fenster: eine zentrierte dunkle Carbon-Karte ueber einem
  abgedunkelten Hintergrund, mit der Ueberschrift als Akzent-Badge oben (vorher nur schlichter Text) und
  CC-Buttons. Ursache war, dass CC die Ausgabeseite gar nicht erkannte (die Erkennung verlangte ein
  Formular, das nach dem Anwenden durch die Ausgabe ersetzt ist) - jetzt hat sie ihre eigene Erkennung.

### 2.64.1
- Fix Dropdowns im "Konfiguration hinzufuegen"-Dialog (Weiteren Pfad/Port/Variable ...): die aufgeklappte
  Liste sass voellig verschoben am rechten Rand und die unteren drei liessen sich gar nicht oeffnen. Ursache:
  der Dialog wird per CSS-transform zentriert, wodurch das frei positionierte Panel sich am Dialog statt am
  Bildschirm ausrichtete. Das Panel rechnet den Versatz jetzt heraus und sitzt in JEDEM Fenster direkt unter
  seinem Feld.
- Fix In diesem Dialog blieb bei einigen Feldern ("Container-Pfad", "Host-Pfad") noch ein Doppelpunkt hinter
  dem Badge stehen (er sass als eigener Textknoten neben dem Badge) - jetzt entfernt.

### 2.64.0
- #10 IPs und Ports GESTOPPTER Container werden jetzt angezeigt. Docker meldet fuer einen gestoppten
  Container keine Ports (und keine Live-IP), darum stand in der Docker-Zuweisungen-Tabelle "invalid IP"
  und "???". Die CC-Engine liest jetzt die KONFIGURIERTEN Werte: die statische IP (ueberlebt einen Stopp,
  z. B. eine br0.x-Adresse) und die veroeffentlichten Ports aus HostConfig.PortBindings (z. B. ein Bridge-
  8080:80). Damit fuellen sich sowohl die Badges in der Docker-Liste als auch die Zuweisungen-Tabelle:
  die IP-Spalte zeigt statt "invalid IP" die echte konfigurierte IP, die Port-Spalte statt "???" die
  Bridge-Ports (kursiv als konfigurierter, nicht Live-Wert markiert). Nur ein zusaetzlicher Inspect je
  gestopptem Container.

### 2.63.0
- Der Plugin-Loeschen-Button (Papierkorb-Icon) ist jetzt VOLL ausgefuellt (solides Rot mit weissem Icon)
  statt nur umrandet - passt zum roten Loesch-Badge und liest sich klarer als Aktion.
- Flaggen-Modus: die Laenderauswahl sitzt jetzt DIREKT in der "Flaggen-Modus"-Zeile, zwischen dem Text und
  seinem Schalter (vorher als eigene Zeile darunter).
- Flaggen-Modus und Regenbogen-Modus schliessen sich jetzt sauber gegenseitig aus: beide Schalter bleiben
  klickbar, und das Einschalten des einen schaltet den anderen automatisch aus (kein Ausgrauen mehr). Eine
  Flagge aus der Auswahl zu waehlen aktiviert den Flaggen-Modus direkt.

### 2.62.2
- Fix Container-Installationsseite: die Felder klebten alle im linken Drittel. Die feste 210px-Label-Spalte
  aus 2.62.1 richtete zwar aus, quetschte die Form aber nach links. Jetzt wie die NATIVE Ansicht: 35%-breite
  Label-Spalte, Labels rechtsbuendig - die Felder sitzen mittig und die ganze Breite wird genutzt.
- #8 Fix Die "Vorlage"-Liste liess sich weiterhin nicht sauber scrollen: das frei positionierte Panel ragte
  ~16px unter den Bildschirmrand (die max-height rechnete das eigene Innenabstand nicht mit), sodass das Ende
  der Scrollleiste abgeschnitten war. Mit box-sizing:border-box + etwas Rand bleibt das Panel komplett sichtbar
  und die lange Liste scrollt sauber. (Die neue Version erzwingt zugleich einen frischen Skript-Cache.)

### 2.62.1
- Fix Container-Installationsseite (Container hinzufuegen): die Felder waren nicht mehr sauber ausgerichtet.
  Die Form besteht aus ~104 EINZELNEN dl-Grids, und die content-breite Label-Spalte hatte jede Zeile eigen
  dimensioniert, sodass jedes Feld an einer anderen x-Position begann. Jetzt eine FIXE Label-Spalte (fasst
  das laengste Label) - alle Felder starten in einer Flucht, die Badges sind rechtsbuendig und sitzen so
  weiterhin direkt neben ihrem Feld.
- #8 Fix Die "Vorlage"-Dropdown-Liste liess sich nicht scrollen: das Panel steckte im scrollbaren
  content-Bereich (overflow:auto) fest und wurde an dessen Rand abgeschnitten. Es oeffnet jetzt als frei
  positioniertes Overlay (position:fixed) am Trigger, mit Hoehe auf den verfuegbaren Platz begrenzt - eine
  lange Vorlagenliste bekommt ihre eigene Scrollleiste und klappt bei wenig Platz nach oben auf.

### 2.62.0
- #11 Waehrend das Plugin-Install- bzw. Container-Update-Fenster streamt, zeigte Unraid am Rand einen
  grellgruenen "Ball-Fall"-Loader (drei #6ab034-Punkte). Diese Punkte tragen jetzt die CC-Akzentfarbe,
  damit die Fortschrittsanzeige zum restlichen Fenster passt statt im hässlichen Gruen zu blinken.

### 2.61.0
- #17/#27 Der Plugin-Deinstallieren-Knopf auf der Plugins-Seite ist jetzt ein einzelnes rotes Papierkorb-
  ICON mit Sicherheitsabfrage - genau wie das Entfernen bei den Containern. Unraids separate Bestaetigungs-
  Checkbox faellt weg (der Knopf war frueher bis zum Anhaken deaktiviert); beim Klick kommt ein CC-Dialog
  "Plugin entfernen?" mit Loeschen/Abbrechen, und erst nach Bestaetigen laeuft die echte Deinstallation
  (Unraids openInstall "plugin remove"). Der Titel-Badge dieses Dialogs ist dank #15 in jedem Fenster
  gleich und lesbar. Ein Klick = Abfrage, kein versehentliches Entfernen mehr.

### 2.60.0
- #15 Das ShipLog-Changelog-Fenster ist jetzt stringent im CC-Design: der oberste Titel-Badge war bei
  aktiver Flaggen-/Rainbow-Palette mit einem sehr dunklen Slot (z. B. dem schwarzen Streifen der Deutschland-
  Flagge) gemalt und verschwand im dunklen Modal ("Badge zu klein / nicht ordentlich"). Zu dunkle Paletten-
  Slots weichen fuer den Titel-Badge jetzt auf den HELLSTEN Slot der Palette aus (bleibt on-theme, z. B. das
  Gold der Flagge), sonst auf den Akzent - so ist der Titel-Badge in JEDEM Fenster lesbar und einheitlich.
- #15 Der Changelog-Inhalt rendert wieder als sauberes Markdown (proportional, Versions-Badges, Listen)
  statt als Monospace-Log: der #21-Terminal-Look ist jetzt auf reine Log-Fenster gescopet (ein pre-Block
  ohne geparste Markdown-Struktur), waehrend das Changelog-pre mit seinen Versions-Ueberschriften
  proportional bleibt. Die Feature-Ueberschriften (frueher riesige 28px-Ueberschrift) werden kompakt.

### 2.59.0
- #21/#11/#14 Die Plugin-Install/Update- und Container-Update-Fenster (.sweet-alert.nchan) stylen ihr
  Streaming-Log jetzt korrekt: das ASCII-READY-Banner + das Log rendern MONOSPACE, linksbuendig und in
  einem dunklen Terminal-Block (CCs Changelog-Markdown-Regel hatte das ASCII vorher kollabiert); die
  Container-Update-Schritte werden zu Carbon-Feldset-Karten mit Akzent-Legende. (Der SL-Changelog-Titel
  #15 und der gruene Progress-Spinner #11 kommen als Nachzug, sobald ich die Fenster live erwische.)

### 2.58.1
- #22 Fix: die VM-Stat-Chips (Speicher/Datentraeger-IO/Netzwerk-IO) erschienen nicht, weil die Stats-
  Tabelle LAZY erst beim Oeffnen ihres Subtabs gerendert wird und der Observer sie verpasste; jetzt am
  stabilen #displaybox gebunden (live bewiesen: Chips erscheinen bei jedem Stats-Update).

### 2.58.0
- #16 Funktionale Badges reagieren jetzt beim Mouseover (ShipLog-Changelog/Update-Chips + Docker-Update-
  Chips heben sich per Helligkeit hervor, lesen sich als klickbar).
- #19 Dezente Animationen: sanfte Einblende-Animation fuer die CC-Popups + weiche Hover/Farb-Uebergaenge
  auf der interaktiven Chrome (bewusst NICHT auf live-aktualisierten Insel-Chips, sonst Flackern).
- #24 Alles davon respektiert prefers-reduced-motion und schaltet unter reduzierter Bewegung ab.
- #22 VM-Nutzungsstatistiken vollstaendiger im CC-Style: Speicher/Datentraeger-IO/Netzwerk-IO als CC-Chips
  (re-render-sicher gewrappt) + die CPU-Pills folgen jetzt dem Rainbow-/Flaggen-Modus statt nur dem Akzent.

### 2.57.0
- #9 Docker-Zuweisungen: das leere quadratische Farbfeld vor jedem Container ist weg -- es war eine
  LEERE Label-Zelle (docker-allocation-dt), die CCs Variablen-Badge-Styling faelschlich zu einem leeren
  Kaestchen gemacht hatte (die Regel verlor per Spezifitaet, jetzt mit Doppelklasse ueberstimmt).
- #10 (offen, ehrlich): IPs/Ports fuer GESTOPPTE Container in der Allokations-Tabelle. Unraid zeigt dort
  "invalid IP"/"???" (es inspiziert nur laufende Container); die konfigurierten Werte liegen weder in der
  Tabelle noch client-seitig abrufbar (Template-XML = 404) -- das braucht CCs Engine als Datenquelle
  und kommt als eigener Schritt.

### 2.56.0
- #7 "Container hinzufuegen"-Formular: die Feld-Badges (Vorlage/Name/Beschreibung/...) sitzen jetzt
  direkt neben ihren Feldern statt weit links (die native Label-Spalte war ~664px breit), und ihre
  komische braune Farbe ist einem sauberen neutralen Chip gewichen (die Akzent-Mischung wurde mit
  warmen Akzentfarben matschig).
- #12 Die Feld-Typ-Icons in den Badges werden ausgeblendet.
- #13 Auf Farb-Variablen-Zeilen schrumpft der 30px-Farbwaehler das Textfeld nicht mehr -- das Feld
  fuellt die Zelle, sodass alle Felder auf dieselbe rechte Kante ausgerichtet sind.
- #8 Das Vorlage-Dropdown ist bereits CC-gestylt und scrollt bei langer Liste (max-height 50vh,
  overflow auto); auf Boxen mit wenigen Templates ist schlicht nichts zu scrollen.

### 2.55.1
- #18 Fix: der Array-Fuellstand-Chip blieb leer, weil die Berechnung beim Laden lief BEVOR /Mains
  Datentraeger-Tabelle geparst war. ccArrFill() versucht es jetzt bis zum Vorhandensein der Tabelle
  erneut (live bewiesen: Insel zeigt "Array 80%").

### 2.55.0
- #18 Status-Insel: der Array-Fuellstand-Chip wird endlich befuellt -- auf /Main berechnet CC die
  groessengewichtete Array-Auslastung und cacht sie (cc.arrfill), sodass die Insel den Wert auf JEDER
  Seite zeigt (Unraid 7.3.x liefert den alten Menue-Balken nicht mehr cross-page).
- #23 NEU: Container-Zaehler-Chip in der Insel -- laufende Container live aus Unraids nchan-Feed
  /sub/dockerload (eine Zeile pro laufendem Container), cross-page; eigener Schalter.
- #6 Kopf-Icons ausblenden richtet die verbliebenen Icons live neu aus (ruecken rechtsbuendig nach) --
  war schon durch den 2.51.0-Hide-Fix abgedeckt, jetzt bestaetigt.
- #29 Netzwerk-Durchsatz-Chip NICHT umgesetzt: RX/TX liefert Unraid nur als Dashboard-Globals, nicht
  cross-page ueber nchan -- bewusst weggelassen statt zu faken.

### 2.54.0
- #5 Anzeige-Einstellungen weiter aufgeraeumt: die kompakte Karte enthaelt jetzt nur noch die 3 nativen
  Kopf-Farben (live-sync); Farbschema/Seitenanzeige/Banner/Favoriten liegen komplett nativ (dort im CC-Stil,
  per Button erreichbar).
- #26 NEU: Suchfeld oben im CC-Einstellungen-Panel (filtert Karten/Zeilen ueber ALLE Reiter) plus ein
  zweistufiger "Alles zuruecksetzen"-Knopf, der alle CC-Einstellungen auf Standard setzt.

### 2.53.0
- #1 Regenbogen-Modus-Toggle repariert: der Schalter sprang nach jedem Klick zurueck auf AUS, weil das
  Theming-Snapshot (accent/rainbow/...) nur EINMAL beim Laden gelesen wurde; jetzt liest render() ihn bei
  jeder Aenderung frisch nach.
- #2 Flaggen-Modus zeigt jetzt die ECHTE Flagge (Muster/Wappen) statt drei Farbbalken -- 195 gebuendelte
  flag-icons-SVGs; die Farbstreifen bleiben nur als Fallback fuer fehlende Codes.
- #3 Die Farbfelder (Rainbow-Palette + Flaggenfarben) fuellen jetzt die ganze Kartenbreite; der Reset-Knopf
  sitzt rechts in einer Flucht mit den Schaltern.
- #4 Die Flaggen-Auswahl sitzt jetzt direkt unter dem Flaggen-Modus-Schalter (ohne "Land waehlen"-Ueberschrift).
- #20 Die Servername-Dropdowns sind jetzt klar als Dropdowns erkennbar (deutlicheres Feld + Pfeil).
- #25 Der Flaggen-Auswaehler ist tastaturbedienbar (Pfeile/Enter/Escape); die Suche matcht Name, Landescode
  und den englischen Namen.
- #28 NEU: Paletten-Presets (Carbon/Nord/Solarized/Dracula/Sunset/Forest) -- ein Klick uebernimmt die Palette.

### 2.52.0
- #1 Anzeige-Einstellungen aufgeraeumt (Option A): der Spiegel aller ~21 nativen Anzeige-Felder in den
  CC-Einstellungen war unuebersichtlich. Jetzt liegt die VOLLSTAENDIGE native Anzeige-Seite wieder an
  ihrem Platz -- aber im CannonadeCommand-Stil (Carbon) -- und CC behaelt nur eine kompakte Karte
  "Anzeige (Unraid, live)" mit Theme, den drei Kopf-Farben, Banner, Tab-Ansicht und Favoriten. Diese
  schalten live auch die native Einstellung mit um.
- #2 Der CC-Stil deckt jetzt auch die nativen /Settings-Unterseiten ab (nicht nur die Werkzeuge), damit
  die wieder eingeblendete Anzeige-Seite und die uebrigen Einstellungsseiten einheitlich aussehen.
- #3 Status-Insel (#13): neuer LIVE-RAM-Balken auf JEDER Seite (aus Unraids nchan-Feed /sub/update1, z.B.
  "RAM 48% -- 15.1 GiB") plus ein defensiver CPU-Last-Balken (blendet sich aus, wenn die Box keine
  CPU-Last meldet). Die Balken tragen jetzt ein Kuerzel (Array / RAM / CPU); neue Schalter je Chip.

### 2.51.0
- #1 Flaggen-Modus komplett ueberarbeitet: eigener Ein-/Aus-Schalter, eigener reaktiver Flaggen-Modus
  und ein eigener Flaggen-Auswaehler mit Farbstreifen (statt Emoji-Abkuerzungen wie "DE"/"AF", die auf
  Windows nicht als Flagge rendern) inkl. Suche ueber rund 195 Laender. Die Flaggenfarben werden
  separat angezeigt. Regenbogen- und Flaggen-Modus schliessen sich gegenseitig aus (einer aktiv -> der
  andere ausgegraut).
- #2 Kopf-Icons-Ausblenden gefixt: die Schalter blenden die Icons jetzt wirklich aus (die Regel verlor
  zuvor per CSS-Spezifitaet gegen eine Sichtbar-Regel) -- live, ohne Neuladen.

### 2.50.0
- #1 NEU: jedes Kopf-Icon oben rechts einzeln ein- und ausblendbar (Einstellungen -> Kopfbereich ->
  Kopf-Icons) -- inklusive Glocke und Menue-Knopf.
- #2 NEU: Schalter "Zustandsanzeigen nativ faerben" (Einstellungen -> Allgemein). AN = Auslastungs-
  balken zeigen ihre Zustandsfarbe (gruen/gelb/rot je Fuellstand); AUS = sie folgen dem Farbmodus
  (Akzent/Regenbogen/Flagge).
- #3 Werkzeug-Unterseiten im CannonadeCommand-Stil: Feldsets als dunkle Karten, Ueberschriften als
  Badges, Tabellen/Formulare/Knoepfe/Log-Ausgaben im Carbon-Look (erste Fassung, wird pro Werkzeug
  weiter verfeinert).
- #4 Das Container-Installations-/Log-Fenster ("Container hinzufuegen") ist jetzt ebenfalls im CC-Stil.
- #5 Kopfbereich robuster: Servername und Glocke richten sich nach dem vollstaendigen Laden neu aus
  (kein kurzes Verrutschen mehr bei breiten Fenstern).

### 2.49.1
- #1 Kopf-Icons perfekt gleichmaessig: die Luecke vom letzten Icon zur Glocke ist jetzt exakt 6px wie
  ueberall (der Abstands-Versuch aus 2.49.0 griff noch nicht -- jetzt misst CC die echte Luecke und
  schiebt sie passgenau auf 6px).
- #2 Docker-Fussleiste genau so breit wie die Container-Liste (statt ueber die volle Fensterbreite).
- #3 Subtabs (z.B. Benutzer- und Datentraegerfreigaben) und Abschnitts-Ueberschriften (Systemein-
  stellungen, Netzwerkdienste ...) sind jetzt ueberall gleich gross.

### 2.49.0
- #1 Anzeige-Einstellungen aufgeraeumt: die lange Theming-Karte ist in drei thematische Karten
  gesplittet (Allgemein / Werte und Einheiten / Kopfbereich und Banner), und JEDE Einstellung hat
  jetzt eine Info-Blase mit Erklaerung.
- #2 Kopfzeilen-Farben (Text, Sekundaertext, Hintergrund) sind als Farbwaehler zurueck, und ein
  eigenes Banner-Bild laesst sich wieder setzen (Knopf oeffnet Unraids Banner-Upload).
- #3 NEU Flaggen-Modus: waehle eine von rund 195 Laenderflaggen und alles faerbt sich in deren
  Flaggenfarben. Der reaktive Regenbogen-Modus wirkt dann als reaktiver Flaggen-Modus.
- #4 Kopf-Icons gleichmaessig beabstandet: die Luecke zwischen dem letzten Icon und der Glocke ist
  jetzt 6px wie ueberall (war 3px).
- #5 Einstellungen/Werkzeuge: das Raster-Icon einer Abschnitts-Ueberschrift (z.B. Systeminformation)
  ist jetzt weiss wie die uebrigen und fuegt sich ein.

### 2.48.1
- #1 Kein Aufblitzen der nativen Oberflaeche mehr beim Seitenaufbau (FOUC): CannonadeCommand setzt
  seinen Stil jetzt schon VOR dem ersten Rendern (synchron im Seitenkopf), statt kurz die native
  Unraid-Ansicht zu zeigen und dann umzuschalten. Rein additiv -- blendet nie Inhalt aus, faellt bei
  Fehlern auf das alte Verhalten zurueck.

### 2.48.0
- #1 Anzeige-Einstellungen komplett in CannonadeCommand gebuendelt: alle Unraid-Anzeige-Optionen
  (Farbschema, Sprache, Schriftgroessen, Zahlen- und Groessenformat, Tabs, Temperatureinheit,
  Banner, Favoriten u.v.m.) erscheinen jetzt live im CC-Tab "Anzeige" und werden nativ gespeichert.
  Die native "Anzeige"-Kachel in den Unraid-Einstellungen wird ausgeblendet -- kein Hin und Her
  mehr, eine Quelle der Wahrheit.
- #2 Benachrichtigungszentrum groesser und geraeumiger: breiteres Fenster, mehr Luft zwischen den
  Meldungen.
- #3 Benachrichtigungs-Aktionen als Badges: "Alle archivieren" und "Alle loeschen" sind jetzt
  Badges statt Text-Links, direkt nebeneinander.
- #4 "Alle loeschen" funktioniert zuverlaessig: leert Ungelesen UND Archiv und aktualisiert die
  Ansicht sofort -- zweistufig abgesichert (erst "Wirklich loeschen?", dann loeschen).
- #5 Kein abseitiges Bestaetigungsfenster mehr beim Archivieren -- Archivieren und Loeschen laufen
  ohne abgesetzten Dialog.

### 2.47.1
- #1 Neuer Schalter "Favoriten-Tab ausblenden" (Einstellungen -> Allgemein): blendet den Favoriten-
  Menue-Tab aus. Unraids eigenes favorites=no blendete ihn NICHT aus (und CC erzwang ihn per Layout-
  Regel sogar sichtbar) -- jetzt zuverlaessig weg, sofort und ohne Neuladen.

### 2.47.0
- #1 Neues finales Logo ueberall (Unraid-Kachel, Kopfbereich, Banner, Einstellungen): drei Kanonen
  im Doppelring -- liest sauber auf jedem Unraid-Theme.
- #2 Kopfbereich: Status-Insel-Chips rechtsbuendig in zwei bis drei Zeilen, die Unraid-Version ist
  jetzt ein echter Insel-Chip (kein separat schwebender mehr); alle Menue-Icons gleich beabstandet.
- #3 Benachrichtigungszentrum als schwebendes CC-Fenster (oben rechts, abgerundet) + neuer
  "Alle loeschen"-Button -- bisher liessen sich Benachrichtigungen nur archivieren.
- #4 Hamburger-Menue vollstaendig im CC-Stil: Warn-Meldung ohne Rahmen, aktiv ausgewaehlter Punkt
  im CC-Akzent statt Farbverlauf.
- #5 Docker-Formular: ALLE Feld-Labels als Badge ohne Doppelpunkt, Pflichtfelder mit rotem Punkt;
  die Badges folgen dem eingestellten Farbmodus (Akzent/Regenbogen).
- #6 Docker-Aktionen: maximal 4 Icons pro Zeile -- auch die per "..."-Expander nachgeladenen --
